hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Waqifi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that he saw the adhan in a dream, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it to him. He said: So Bilal gave the adhan. He said: And my uncle came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see the dream while Bilal gives the adhan! He said: So you give the iqama. He said: So my uncle gave the iqama."
"1202","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Mu'awiya ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about omens, and he said: It is something you find in your breasts, so let it not turn you back. I said: O Messenger of Allah, there are people who go to soothsayers! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not go to them."
"1203","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad and Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymuna, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Mu'awiya ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man beside me sneezed, so I said: May Allah have mercy on you! So the people stared at me, and I said: May my mother lose me, why do you look at me while I am praying! So they began striking their hands upon their thighs to silence me, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, may my father and mother be ransomed for him, I never saw before him nor after him anyone better in teaching than him; by Allah, he neither scolded me nor insulted me nor struck me, but said to me: This prayer of ours, nothing of human speech is proper in it; it is only prayer, glorification, praise, and recitation of the Quran, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. And I had sheep grazing between Uhud and al-Jawwaniya with a slave girl of mine among them, and one day I looked and found a wolf had taken a sheep from them, and I am of the children of Adam regretting as they regret, so I raised my hand and struck her a blow, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he regarded it gravely for me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not free her? He said: Call her. So I called her. He said: So he said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Free her, for she is a believer. I said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are people who draw lines! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was a prophet among the prophets who drew lines, so whoever agrees with his line, that is it. I said: Among us are people who take omens. He said: It is something they find in their breasts, but let it not turn them back. I said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are people who go to soothsayers. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not go to them."
"1204","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hashraj ibn Nubata narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Jumhan narrated to us, from Safina, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: There was no prophet except that he warned his community of the Dajjal; indeed he is blind in the left eye, with a thick growth over the right, with disbeliever written between his eyes, meaning written: kaf-fa-ra. And with him will come two valleys, one appearing as Paradise and the other as Fire, so his fire is Paradise and his Paradise is Fire. The Dajjal will say to the people: Am I not your lord, giving life and death? And with him are two prophets whose names and whose fathers' names I know; if I wished I could name them, one on his right and the other on his left. So he says: Am I not your lord, giving life and death? Then one of them says: You lie, but none of the people hears him except his companion, and the other says: You speak truth, and the people hear him, and that is a trial. Then he will travel until he comes to Madina and says: This is the town of that man, but he will not be permitted to enter it. Then he will travel until he comes to Sham, and Allah will destroy him at the pass of Afiq."
"1205","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hashraj ibn Nubata narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Jumhan narrated to me, saying: Safina narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: The caliphate in my community is thirty years, then there will be kingship. Then Safina said: Count: the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and the caliphate of Umar, twelve years and six months, and the caliphate of Uthman, twelve years, then the caliphate of Ali completing the thirty. I said: And Mu'awiya? He said: He was the first of the kings."
"1206","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws ibn Hudhayfa al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from his grandfather Aws, who said: We came as the delegation of Thaqif to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the confederates lodged with al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba and he lodged the Malikites in his tent. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to us and speak to us after the last evening prayer, standing so long he would shift between his feet, and most of what he spoke to us of was complaint of Quraysh, saying: We were in Makka humiliated and weak, then when we came to Madina we evened with the people, and the fortunes of war were against us and for us. One night he was held back from us from the time he used to come to us, then he came to us, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you were held back from us tonight from the time you used to come to us! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A portion of the Quran came upon me, and I wished not to go out until I recited it, or he said: completed it. He said: When morning came we asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the divisions of the Quran, how do you divide it? They said: Three, five, seven, nine, eleven, thirteen, and the portion of al-Mufassal."
"1207","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Ibn Aws, whose grandfather was Aws, who said: My grandfather gestured to me to hand him his sandals while he was praying, so I handed them to him and he wore them while praying, and when he finished praying he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"1208","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, who was among the delegation, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a tent with no one of the people awake except me, when a man came and spoke privately with him, and he said: Go and kill him. Then he called him back and said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah; when they testify it they have protected their blood and wealth from me, or he said: they are protected, except by its right."
"1209","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, from Ibn Aws, from his grandfather, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pour forth three times. I said: What is pour forth three times? He said: He poured upon his hand three times."
"1210","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughira al-Ta'ifi, from Aws al-Thaqafi, who said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the delegation of Thaqif and stayed with him half a month, and I saw him turning away to his right and to his left."
"1211","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Aws al-Thaqafi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his sandals."
"1212","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Azdi, from Aws ibn Abi Aws al-Thaqafi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes on Friday and bathes and comes early and arrives in time and walks and does not ride, for every step will be the fast and standing of a year."
"1213","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Umari and Ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'ba on the day of the conquest of Makka and closed the door upon himself, and al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Uthman ibn Talha, Usama ibn Zayd, and Bilal entered with him. When they came out I raced the people and outran them, and said to Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars facing the notch."
"1214","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating that Bilal said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the leather socks and the head covering. And al-A'mash narrated this hadith from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujra, from Bilal."
"1215","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, who said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab narrating from Bilal, the caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We were forbidden only prayer before sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, or he said: upon the two horns of Satan."
"1216","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed a man being cupped, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"1217","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: Two traits I retained from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Allah loves excellence in all things; when you slaughter, slaughter well, and when you kill, kill well; let one sharpen his blade and let his slaughtered animal rest."
"1218","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays to show off has associated, and whoever fasts to show off has associated, and whoever gives charity to show off has associated. So Awf ibn Malik said: Will Allah not take what was for Him of that and accept it and leave the rest? Shaddad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah said: I am the best of partners; whoever associates with Me, his deed, little and much, is for My partner, and I am free of it."
"1219","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ghanm narrated to me that Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him: The worst of this community will surely follow those before them exactly as one sandal thong matches another."
"1220","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Damra ibn Habib, from Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The intelligent one is he who takes account of himself and works for what is after death, and the helpless one is he who makes himself follow his desires and wishes upon Allah."
"1221","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Sumayr narrated to me, saying: Bashir ibn Nuhayk narrated to me, saying: Bashir the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Bashir ibn al-Khasasiya, narrated to me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had named him Bashir, while his name before that was Zahm."
"1222","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Sumayr narrated to us, saying: Bashir ibn Nuhayk narrated to me, saying: Bashir the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Bashir ibn al-Khasasiya, narrated to me, saying: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) holding his hand, or he said holding my hand, he said to me: O son of al-Khasasiya, what complaint have you against Allah this morning? This morning you walk with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: I have no complaint against Allah for anything, may my father and mother be ransomed for you; Allah has done all good to me, all good Allah has done to me. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon the graves of the polytheists and said: These have missed much good, these have missed much good. Then he came upon the graves of the Muslims and said: These have attained much good, these have attained much good. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glanced and saw a man walking among the graves in sandals, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O wearer of the two leather sandals, cast off your two sandals. And when he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he threw them off."
"1223","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit al-Sadusi narrated to us, from his father, from Layla the wife of Bashir ibn al-Khasasiya, who said: I intended to fast two days continuously, so I mentioned that to Bashir, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it and said: The Jews do that, but fast, and when night comes then break the fast."
"1224","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Umama, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came to him with a boy of hers, or two boys of hers whom she was carrying, and another small son, and I think she was pregnant, and I think she did not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day for anything except that he gave it to her. When she turned away the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Carrying, bearing, merciful women; were it not for what they do toward their husbands, those of them who pray would enter Paradise."
"1225","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us, having heard Abu Umama saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Farewell Pilgrimage and heard him saying: Allah has given every possessor of a right his right, so there is no bequest for an heir; the child belongs to the bed and the adulterer gets the stone; their account is upon Allah. Whoever claims sonship to other than his father or attaches himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah continuing until the Day of Resurrection. No woman may give anything of her husband's wealth except with his permission. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, not even food? He said: That is the best of our wealth."
"1226","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to us, having heard Abu Umama saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A debt is to be paid, a borrowed item is to be returned, a granted benefit is to be given back, and the guarantor is liable."
"1227","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ablution expiates what came before it, and the prayer becomes supererogatory. So it was said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: More than once, not twice, not three times, not four, not five."
"1228","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created creation, decreed the decree, took the covenant of the prophets, while His Throne was upon the water; so the people of Paradise are its people, and the people of Hell are its people."
"1229","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the disobedient to parents, nor the reminder of favors, nor the denier of destiny will enter Paradise."
"1230","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Ayman, from Abu Umama, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Blessed is he who saw me and believed in me, and blessed seven times is he who did not see me and believed in me."
"1231","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the most enviable people to me is a servant with a share of prayer who obeys his Lord and increases his worship in secret, who is not pointed at with fingers, who is obscure among people, whose livelihood is suffices, whose death comes quickly, whose inheritance is little and whose mourners are few."
"1232","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Faraj ibn Fudala narrated to us, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Yazid ibn Mu'awiya, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sent me as guidance and mercy to the worlds, and commanded me to eradicate stringed instruments, flutes, idols, crosses, and the affairs of ignorance. And my Lord swore by His might and majesty: No servant of Mine drinks a draught of wine deliberately in this world except that I shall give him to drink instead of it from pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether forgiven or punished; and he does not give it to drink to a weak young Muslim except that I shall give him to drink instead of it from pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether forgiven or punished; and he does not leave it out of fear of Me except that I shall give him it to drink in the enclosure of holiness. Their sale is not lawful, nor their purchase, nor trading in them, and their price is unlawful."
"1233","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umama, who said: When a Muslim performs ablution and performs it well, if he sits he sits forgiven, and if he prays it is a merit for him. So it was said to him: Or supererogatory? He said: Supererogatory deeds were only for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1234","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, who said: I was with Abu Umama when heads of the Khawarij were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus, and he said: Dogs of Hell, he said it three times, the worst slain killed under the shade of the sky; the best slain are those whom they kill and who kill them, he said it three times. I said: Something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or something you say from your opinion? He said: If so I would be audacious, if so I would be audacious; rather something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1235","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Farqad, from Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali, from Abu Umama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A people of this community will spend the night upon food and drink and amusement and play, then wake having been transformed into monkeys and pigs; and they will surely be struck by collapse and pelting until people wake saying: Last night such-and-such tribe was swallowed, and last night such-and-such house was swallowed; and He will surely send upon them a storm of stones from heaven as was sent upon the people of Lut, upon some tribes of them and upon some houses; and He will surely send upon them the barren wind that destroyed Ad, upon some tribes among them and upon some houses, because of their drinking wine, wearing silk, taking singing women, consuming usury, and severing kinship; and a trait which Ja'far forgot."
"1236","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the two leather socks on his feet in the expedition of Tabuk for three days."
"1237","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from a shaykh, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellent, excellent; five, how heavy they are: glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and a righteous child who dies and his parent seeks reward for him."
"1238","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Faraj ibn Fudala narrated to us, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Abu Umama, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what was the beginning of your matter? He said: The supplication of my father Ibrahim and the glad tidings of Isa son of Maryam, and my mother saw that a light emerged from her illuminating the palaces of Sham."
"1239","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man was taken to the gate of Paradise and raised his head, and upon the gate of Paradise was written: Charity is tenfold its like, and a single loan is eighteenfold; for the borrower does not come to you except in need, while charity may be placed with a rich man."
"1240","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a narrating from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing, saying: There is no servant who sends blessings upon me except that the angels send blessings upon him as long as he sends blessings upon me, so let the servant do little or much."
"1241","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Ubaydullah informed me, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a narrating from his father that a woman of Fazara was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having married a man for two sandals, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Are you content with yourself and your wealth for two sandals? She said: Yes, so he permitted it."
"1242","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a, from his father, who said: I cannot count, or he said how often, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the tooth-stick while fasting."
"1243","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Ash'ath ibn Sa'id Abu al-Rabi' and Umar ibn Qays said: Asim ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a, from his father, who said: It once became dark while we were on a journey and the qibla became unclear to us, so each man of us prayed in his own direction; when it cleared, some of us had prayed toward other than the qibla and some toward the qibla, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Your prayer has passed, and there was revealed: So wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah."
"1244","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in circumambulation when his sandal strap broke, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, hand it to me to mend! He said: This is preferring oneself, and I do not love preferring."
"1245","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, having heard Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning fasting a lifetime: He neither fasted nor broke fast."
"1246","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif, from his father, who said: I came upon the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reciting: Rivalry in increase distracted you, and he was saying: The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth; and have you, O son of Adam, of your wealth except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent forth!"
"1247","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Judi al-Shami informed me, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Muhajir narrating from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, who had companionship, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who stays as guest with a people and the guest wakes deprived except that it is upon every Muslim to aid him until he takes his night's hospitality from their crops and wealth."
"1248","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Budayl, who said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talha narrating from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever leaves wealth it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves a burden it is to us, and perhaps he said: to Allah and His Messenger; and I am the heir of him who has no heir, paying blood money on his behalf and inheriting him, and the maternal uncle is heir of him who has no heir, paying on his behalf and inheriting him."
"1249","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Abu Karima, having heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The guest's night is a right upon every Muslim; whoever wakes with the guest at his courtyard, it is a right upon him, or he said a debt; if he wishes he exacts it and if he wishes he leaves it."
"1250","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jalil ibn Atiya narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Amr ibn Abasa al-Sulami, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever grows a white hair in Islam, or he said in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection, as long as he does not dye it or pluck it. I said to Shahr: They dye yellow and dye with henna? He said: Yes, as though meaning black."
"1251","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from a man of the jurists of Sham, from Amr ibn Abasa, who said: You have seen me when I was a fourth of Islam; I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who followed you in this matter? He said: A free man and a slave, meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal."
"1252","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talha al-Ya'mari, from Abu Najih al-Sulami, who said: We besieged the fortress of Ta'if with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever hits with an arrow in the path of Allah, it equals a freed slave for him, so that day I hit sixteen arrows. Then I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, it is a rank for him in Paradise; and whoever grows a white hair in Islam it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection; and any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, Allah will make protection for every bone of his bones freed from the Fire; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, Allah will make protection for every bone of her bones freed from the Fire."
"1253","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd al-Shami, who said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir saying: There was a treaty between Mu'awiya and the Romans, so he would travel in their lands until, when the treaty ended, he would raid them, when a man on a mount, or on a horse, said: Allah is greatest, fidelity not treachery, twice, and behold it was Amr ibn Abasa al-Sulami. So Mu'awiya said to him: What do you say? So Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever has a treaty between him and a people should neither loosen a knot nor tighten it until its term passes or he renounces it to them upon equality. So Mu'awiya returned with the people."
"1254","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrating from his father, from al-Ashtar, who said: There were words between Ammar and Khalid ibn al-Walid, so Ammar complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Khalid, whoever shows enmity to Ammar, Allah shows enmity to him; whoever hates him, Allah hates him; and whoever reviles Ammar, Allah reviles him. Salama said this or its like."
"1255","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Najih, from Khalid ibn Hakim, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are those most severe in punishing people in this world."
"1256","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: We were sitting in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when people came praising Uthman and extolling him, while al-Miqdad was in a corner of the mosque; when he heard them praising him he stood and took pebbles and began throwing them in their faces. So Uthman said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you see those who praise extravagantly, throw dust in their faces, or he said in their mouths, or he said pebbles."
"1257","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, who said: A man began praising a boy of Uthman, so al-Miqdad went and began throwing dust in his face. So Uthman said to him: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you see those who praise extravagantly, throw dust in their faces."
"1258","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, saying: I came with two companions of mine whose hearing and sight were almost gone from hardship, and we began presenting ourselves to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with none accepting us, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took us to his dwelling, and the family of Muhammad had three goats they would milk. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would distribute the milk among us, and we would set aside the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would come and greet with a greeting that made the awake hear without waking the sleeper. Then Satan said to me: If only you drank this draught! For the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) goes to the Ansar and they give him gifts. He kept at it until I drank it, and when I drank it he made me regret, saying: What have you done? Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come and not find his drink, and will supplicate against you and you will perish. As for my two companions, they drank their drink and slept, while I could not sleep, with a woolen cloak of mine that, when I put it on my head my feet showed, and when I put it on my feet my head showed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came as he used to come, prayed as much as Allah willed him to pray, then looked at his drink and saw nothing, so he raised his hand. I said: He will supplicate against me now and I shall perish! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, feed whoever fed me and give drink to whoever gave me drink. So I took the knife and the cloak and went to the goats feeling them to see which was fattest to slaughter for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behold all were full-uddered. So I took a vessel of the family of Muhammad, one they would not hope to milk into, and milked until the foam rose over it, then brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he drank, then handed it to me and I drank, then I handed it to him and he drank, then he handed it to me and I drank, then I laughed until I fell to the ground. So he said to me: One of your misdeeds, O Miqdad. Then I began telling him what I had done, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It was only a mercy from Allah; if only you had awakened your two companions so they could have had some of it! So I said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I do not care, once you have had it and I have had your excess, who among people missed it."
"1259","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from al-Harith al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah revealed to Yahya son of Zakariya five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon, but he seemed slow with them, so Allah revealed to Isa: Either convey them or he conveys them. So Isa came to him and said: Allah commanded you with five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon, so either you inform them or I inform them! He said: O Spirit of Allah, do not do it, for I fear if you precede me with them I shall be swallowed or punished! He said: So he gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was full and they sat upon the terraces, then he addressed them saying: Allah revealed to me five words and commanded the Children of Israel to act upon them; the first: not to associate anything with Allah, for the likeness of one who associates with Allah is like a man who bought a slave with his pure wealth for gold or silver, then settled him in a house and said: Work and render to me, but the slave rendered to other than his master; which of you would be pleased that his slave be so? For Allah created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with Him; and when you stand for prayer do not turn away, for Allah turns His Face to the face of His servant as long as he does not turn; and He commanded you with fasting, whose likeness is like a man among a group with a pouch of musk, all loving to find its scent, and the breath of the fasting one's mouth to Allah is sweeter than the scent of musk; and He commanded you with charity, whose likeness is like a man captured by the enemy who bound him by his neck or brought him near to strike his neck, and he said to them: Will you let me ransom myself from you, and gave little and much until he ransomed himself; and He commanded you with much remembrance of Allah, whose likeness is like a man pursued swiftly by the enemy in his tracks until he came to a fortified fortress and secured himself therein; likewise the servant is not saved from Satan except by remembrance of Allah."
"1260","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from al-Harith, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I command you with five which Allah commanded me with: unity, hearing and obedience, emigration, and striving in the path of Allah; whoever separates from the community by a handspan has cast off the bond of Islam, or faith, from his neck, or faith from his head, unless he returns; and whoever calls with the call of ignorance is of the heaps of Hell. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: Even if he fasts and prays; call with the call of Allah by which He named you: Muslims, believers, servants of Allah."
"1261","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for the front row three times and for the second once."
"1262","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, having heard Abdullah ibn Salima narrating from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi that two men of the People of the Book, one said to his companion: Let us go to this Prophet. The other said: Let him not hear this and gain four eyes. So they came to him and asked him about nine clear signs, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not associate anything with Allah, do not kill, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not practice magic, do not consume usury, do not slander the chaste woman, do not flee from battle, do not walk with an innocent one to a ruler to kill or destroy him; and upon you in particular, O Jews, not to transgress on the Sabbath. So they kissed his hands and feet and said: We testify you are a prophet. He said: What prevents you from following me? They said: Dawud supplicated that there always be a prophet among his offspring, and we fear if we follow you the Jews will kill us! And Abu Dawud once said: Nor slander the chaste woman, or: nor flee from battle; Abu Dawud said: Shu'ba doubted."
"1263","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama, Hammad ibn Zayd, Hammam, and Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I went in the morning to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, and he said: What brought you, O Zirr? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salama said it, and none of them said it, and he raised the hadith: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks."
"1264","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama, Hammad ibn Zayd, Hammam, and Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, who said: I went in the morning to Safwan ibn Assal and said: Something about wiping over the leather socks troubled me, have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, or traveling, and he commanded us to wipe over them three days and their nights for stool, urine, and sleep, except for major impurity."
"1265","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba, Hammad ibn Salama, Hammad ibn Zayd, and Hammam narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, who said: I said to Safwan ibn Assal: Have you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about love? He said: Yes; we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a march or expedition when a Bedouin called him with a loud voice, saying: O Muhammad, O Muhammad, O Muhammad. It was said to him: Woe to you, lower your voice, you have been forbidden raising your voice! He kept calling thus until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him in like manner, saying: Here I am. He said: What of a man who loves people but has not joined them! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves."
"1266","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba, Hammad ibn Salama, Hammad ibn Zayd, and Hammam narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: Safwan kept narrating to me until he mentioned the gate of repentance toward the west, its width forty years, or a journey of forty years, remaining open until the sun rises from it, and that is His saying: The day some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"1267","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abbad ibn Shurahbil, who said: I came to Madina gripped by severe hunger, so I entered a garden and took an ear of grain, ate from it and put some in my garment. The owner of the garden came, beat me and took what was in my garment. So we went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You neither taught him when he was ignorant, nor fed him when he was hungry. So he ordered for me half a wasq of barley."
"1268","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fudala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Taghlib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me a word I would not love to have red camels for: captives were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave to some people and withheld from some. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We give to people fearing their panic and distress, and we entrust people to the faith Allah has placed in their hearts, among them Amr ibn Taghlib."
"1269","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fudala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: And Amr ibn Taghlib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among the signs of the Hour is that you fight a people whose sandals are hair; and among the signs of the Hour is that you fight a people whose faces are as hammered shields; and among the signs of the Hour is that traders increase and the pen appears."
"1270","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, who said: Rabi'a ibn Ka'b al-Aslami narrated to me, saying: I spent the night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), handing him ablution water at night, and through the night I would hear him saying: Allah hears whoever praises Him, and through the night I would hear him saying: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1271","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mubarak ibn Fudala narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Rabi'a ibn Ka'b, who said: I used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one day he said: O Rabi'a, will you not marry? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I have nothing to sustain a wife, and I do not wish anything to distract me from your service. Then he said to me another day: O Rabi'a, will you not marry? So I said the like to him. He said: Then I said to myself: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah knows better what is good for me in my world and hereafter than I do; by Allah, if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says it a third time I shall surely say yes. So he said to me a third time: O Rabi'a, will you not marry? He said: I said: Let the Messenger of Allah do as he wills. So he said: Go to the family of so-and-so, people of the Ansar, and say: The Messenger of Allah sent me conveying greetings and commanding you to marry me to so-and-so. So I went to them and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to marry me to so-and-so. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah; by Allah, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah shall not return today except with his need. He said: So they married me and honored me, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me gloomy and sad, and said: What is wrong with you, O Rabi'a? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to noble people who honored me and married me, but I have nothing for a dower! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Burayda al-Aslami, gather for me the weight of a date-stone in gold. So he gathered it for me, and he said: Go with this to them. So I went to them, and they accepted it from me and rejoiced. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw me gloomy, and said: What is wrong with you, O Rabi'a? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to noble people who accepted it from me and rejoiced, but I have nothing for a wedding feast! He said: O Burayda, gather for him the price of a ram. So they gathered for me the price of a great ram, then he said: Go to A'isha and say to her: The Messenger of Allah says to you: Hand over to him that food. So I went to her and she said: Here is the basket; by Allah, we have nothing else. He said: So I took it and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Go with this to them; let this be prepared with them as bread and this be cooked with them as meat. So I brought it to them, and they said: As for bread we shall suffice you, and you suffice us the meat. So I went with the ram to some companions of mine and we cooperated upon it, finished it, went with it and made the feast, invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he accepted my invitation."
"1272","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mubarak ibn Fudala narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Rabi'a ibn Ka'b al-Aslami, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me land and gave Abu Bakr land. We differed over a cluster, meaning a palm tree; I said: It is of my land! And Abu Bakr said: It is of my land! He said: O Abu Bakr, do you not see? Look, do you not see? It is of my land! But he refused, and said to me a word he regretted, saying: O Rabi'a, say to me the like of what I said to you so it be retaliation! He said: I said: No. He said: Then he said: By Allah, I shall surely seek judgment against you! He said: I said: You may. So he set out toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I followed him, and people of my tribe came, saying: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr, he is the one who said to you what he said and seeks judgment against you! So they went with me, and I said to them: Do you know who this is? This is Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the second of two when they were in the cave; he comes to the Messenger of Allah angry, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will become angry for his anger, and Allah will become angry for the anger of His Messenger, and Rabi'a will perish; go back! So I sent them back and went on, while he had preceded me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. When I came he said to me: O Rabi'a, what is between you and al-Siddiq? I said: O Messenger of Allah, he said something to me, and said to me: Say the like of what I said to you so it be retaliation, but I said: I shall not say to you the like of what you said to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, so do not say to him the like of what he said to you, but say: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr. So I said: May Allah forgive you, Abu Bakr; may Allah forgive you, Abu Bakr. He said: So Abu Bakr turned away weeping."
"1273","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Hamza al-Aslami, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling? He said: If you wish then fast, and if you wish then break fast."
"1274","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Jarhad, from Jarhad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he had uncovered his thigh, and said: O Jarhad, cover your thigh, for it is of the private area."
"1275","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam al-Saluli informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Hawra al-Sa'di, saying: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: What do you remember of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I took a date of charity dates and put it in my mouth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed it with its saliva and threw it among the dates. They said: O Messenger of Allah, a date from a boy! He said: We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us."
"1276","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Hawra, saying: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: What do you remember of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to say: Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt; for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt."
"1277","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Burayd informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Hawra, saying: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: What do you remember of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He taught us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, grant me well-being among those You granted well-being, befriend me among those You befriended, protect me from the evil of what You decreed; indeed You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed he whom You befriend is never humbled; blessed are You our Lord and exalted."
"1278","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Sarjis, who had heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended travel he would say: I seek refuge in Allah from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, loss after gain, the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight in wealth and family."
"1279","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Muhammad ibn Safwan that he hunted a rabbit and slaughtered it with a flint, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he commanded him to eat it."
"1280","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I heard Hafsa bint Sirin narrating from al-Rabab, from Salman ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fasts let him break fast upon dates, and if he does not find then upon water, for it is purifying."
"1281","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Khalid ibn Qariz, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, who said: A physician asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a frog he would put in medicine, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from killing it."
"1282","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadla, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hoards except a sinner."
"1283","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Ma'mar narrated to me, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him saying: Look to Quraysh, hear their word and leave their deed."
"1284","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad Abu Sahl, from his father, who said: I saw Muhammad ibn Maslama looking at a woman from above a roof, gazing at her, so I said to him: Do you do this while you are of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah casts proposing to a woman into the heart of one of you, there is no harm in looking at her."
"1285","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Mu'ayqib, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping the pebbles, and he said to me: Once, or leave it."
"1286","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, saying: al-Zubayr ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather. Abu Dawud said: And I heard a shaykh in Makka saying: Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Ujayr, from Rukana ibn Abd Yazid, who said: I had a wife called Suhayya, and I divorced her irrevocably. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I divorced Suhayya irrevocably, but by Allah I intended only one! He said: By Allah, did you intend only one? I said: By Allah, I intended only one! He said: By Allah, did you intend only one? I said: By Allah, I intended only one! So he returned her to me as one."
"1287","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sakan ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, from Farqad Abu Talha, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbab, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urging giving for the army of hardship, so Uthman ibn Affan stood and said: One hundred camels with their saddles and harness in the path of Allah. Then he urged a second time, so Uthman stood and said: Two hundred camels with their saddles and harness in the path of Allah. Then he urged a third time, so Uthman stood and said: Three hundred camels with their saddles and harness in the path of Allah. He said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descending from the minbar saying: Whatever Uthman does after this will not harm him, twice or thrice."
"1288","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from his paternal aunt, from her paternal uncle, who said: I was walking with a cloak of mine trailing, when a man said: Raise your garment, for it is more Godfearing and more lasting. I looked, and behold it was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is only a striped cloak! He said: Do you not have an example in me? Then I looked, and his lower garment reached half his shin."
"1289","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating from Abdullah ibn Rabi'a, who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Khalid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between two men; one was killed and the other remained, then he died and they prayed over him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you say? They said: We supplicated Allah to forgive him, have mercy on him, and join him with his companion. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then where is his prayer after his prayer? And where is his deed after his deed? And I think he said: And where is his fast after his fast? By Him in whose Hand is my soul, what is between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth. Amr ibn Maymun said: This hadith pleased me because it was narrated to me with a chain."
"1290","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Suwayd ibn Qays, who said: I and Makhrafa brought cloth from Hajar, and I sold trousers to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a weigher weighing for a wage. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Weigh and give excess."
"1291","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Simak, who said: I heard Abu Safwan Malik ibn Umayr saying: I sold the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a leg of trousers before the emigration for three dirhams, and he weighed for me and gave excess."
"1292","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Hatib saying: A pot fell upon my hand and it burned, so my mother took me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he began spitting upon it and saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind; and I think he said: And heal, You are the Healer."
"1293","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Simak ibn Harb informed me, saying: I heard Tha'laba ibn al-Hakam al-Laythi saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when sheep were plundered, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, and the pots were overturned."
"1294","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, having heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Ibn Labid, a man of the Ansar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the time of the departure of knowledge, or: this is the time of the cessation of knowledge. So Ibn Labid said: O Messenger of Allah, how, when among us is the Book of Allah, we teach it to our children and our children teach it to their children? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May your mother lose you, O Ibn Labid, I used to consider you the most intelligent man in Madina; were not the Jews and Christians given the Torah and Gospel, yet they benefited nothing from that?"
"1295","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, who said: Thabit ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer is not bound by a vow over what he does not own; cursing a believer is like killing him; whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam is as he said."
"1296","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, who said: It was said to Ka'b ibn Murra, or Murra ibn Ka'b al-Bahzi: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may Allah honor your father, and beware! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, it is his ransom from the Fire; for every bone of his bones a bone of his bones is recompensed; and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they are his ransom from the Fire; for every two bones of theirs a bone of his is recompensed; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she is her ransom from the Fire; for every bone of hers a bone of hers is recompensed."
"1297","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Salim, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Ka'b ibn Murra, or Murra ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar, so I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has aided you, given you, and answered you, yet your people have perished, so supplicate Allah for them! He said: So he said: O Allah, give us rain, relieving, wholesome, fruitful, covering, abundant, immediate without delay, beneficial without harm. He said: It was not the next Friday or thereabouts before we were rained upon."
"1298","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, that Ka'b ibn Murra said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from people whose camels do not stir for them and whose shepherd does not provision for them."
"1299","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, saying: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf, saying: I heard Amr ibn Rashid, from Wasiba ibn Ma'bad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone in the row and commanded him to repeat the prayer."
"1300","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, having heard Abu Burda narrating that he heard a man of Juhayna called al-Agharr narrating to Ibn Umar that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him a hundred times a day."
"1301","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Khalid ibn Arfaja al-Ashja'i, who said: They were traveling with Salim ibn Ubayd al-Ashja'i when a man sneezed and said: Peace be upon you! So Salim said: And upon you and upon your mother! Then he traveled a while, then said to the man: Perhaps you disliked what I said to you? He said: I wished you had not mentioned my mother with good or evil! He said: I only narrate to you what I witnessed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a man sneezed before him and said: Peace be upon you! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you and upon your mother; when one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, or: Praise be to Allah in every state; and let his brother say to him: May Allah have mercy on you; and let him say: May Allah forgive me and you."
"1302","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Qays ibn Abi Gharaza, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us in the market while we were selling measures, and we called ourselves brokers, so he named us with a name better than what we named ourselves."
"1303","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Wa'il, from Qays ibn Abi Gharaza, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O assembly of traders, idle talk and oaths mix into this market of yours, so mix it with charity, or with something of charity."
"1304","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Dirghama ibn Ulayba ibn Harmala al-Anbari narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the riders of the tribe, and he led us in the dawn prayer, and I began looking at the one beside me, hardly recognizing him, from the darkness."
"1305","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra narrated to us, saying: Dirghama narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among riders of the tribe, and when I wanted to return I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me! He said: Fear Allah; and when you are in a gathering and rise from them, and hear them saying what pleases you, then come to it; and when you hear them saying what you dislike, then do not come to it."
"1306","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Sulaym al-Hujaymi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting with his knees drawn up in a cloak of his, as if I can still see its fringes upon his feet, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me! He said: Fear Allah, and do not belittle any good deed, even pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one seeking water, and meeting your brother with a cheerful face toward him. And beware of letting the lower garment hang below the ankles, for letting it hang is from pride and Allah does not love it. And if a man reviles you and reproaches you for something that is in you, do not reproach him for something that is in him; leave him, his evil consequence will be upon him and its reward will be for you. And never revile anything. He said: So after the words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I never reviled an animal nor a human being."
"1307","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Asas ibn Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and missed a man among his Companions, so he was brought to him and he said: I wanted to devote myself to the worship of my Lord and withdraw from people! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do it, and let none of you do it - he said it three times - for enduring patiently for an hour in one of the stations of the Muslims is better than forty years of worship in seclusion."
"1308","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari, from Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited: {When the sun is folded up}, and when he came to this verse: {And the night as it darkens, and the morning as it brightens}, I said to myself: What is the night when it darkens and the morning when it breathes?"
"1309","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, who said: We used to fast Ashura and give Zakat al-Fitr before the fast of Ramadan and zakat were revealed upon us, then when they were revealed we were neither commanded concerning them nor forbidden from them, and we used to do them."
"1310","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Yazid saying: I never saw anyone who enjoined fasting Ashura more than Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abu Musa, may Allah have mercy on them both."
"1311","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi. Abu Dawud said: And Ibn Fadalah informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of the Asd tribe for work - or he said: for charity - and when he came he came with two amounts of wealth and said: This is your wealth, and this is a gift given to me. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood to deliver a sermon, then said: What is the matter with men whom we send for some of what Allah has entrusted to us, then one comes with two amounts and says: This is your wealth and this is a gift given to me; would he not sit in the house of his father or in the house of his mother and see whether he is given gifts or not? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no one takes anything from this wealth without right except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it upon his neck; if it was a camel he will come with it bellowing, and if it was a cow he will come with it mooing, and if it was a sheep it will come bleating. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, bear witness. Abu Humayd said: My very eyes saw and my ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the witness to that is Zayd ibn Thabit, my knee rubbing against his knee in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1312","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu Sayyarah al-Mutai, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bees! He said: Pay the tenth. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, reserve its mountain for me! So he reserved it for me."
"1313","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh, he said: Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm - and he is a clan of Ghifar - narrated to me, he said: I was present at Khaybar with my master, and when it was conquered I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to allot a share for me, so he refused to allot a share for me and gave me from the lowly household goods."
"1314","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Ushara, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the upper chest or the throat? He said: If you stabbed it in its thigh it would suffice for you. Abu Dawud said: Meaning for one that fell into a well."
"1315","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Amr ibn Kharijah, who said: I was beneath the neck of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it was bringing up its cud, and its saliva was flowing between my shoulders, and I heard him saying: Allah has given every one who has a right his right, and no bequest is permitted for an heir. The child belongs to the marital bed, and the adulterer gets the stone. And whoever claims to belong to other than his father or attaches himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither an optional nor an obligatory deed will be accepted from him."
"1316","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made wiping for the traveler three, and had we asked for more he would have given us more."
"1317","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning wiping over the leather socks: For the resident a day and a night, and for the traveler three days and their nights."
"1318","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Thabit ibn Wadiah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard and said: A nation that was transformed, and Allah knows best."
"1319","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali saying: I witnessed Thabit ibn Wadiah and Qarazah ibn Kab al-Ansari at a wedding feast, and there was singing, so I spoke to them about that, and they said: Singing at weddings and weeping over the dead without wailing has been permitted."
"1320","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed me, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani narrating from Thabit ibn Wadiah, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a lizard and placed it before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A nation that was transformed, and I do not know, perhaps this is of them."
"1321","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, he said: I heard Muadhah narrating from Hisham ibn Amir al-Ansari - of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to sever ties with his brother for more than three days, for the two of them are turned away from the truth so long as they remain in severance, and the first of them to return, his precedence in returning will be an expiation for him. And if he greets him and he does not accept his greeting and returns his greeting, the angels return it upon him and a devil returns it upon the other. And if they both die in their severance, they will not enter Paradise - or he said: They will never be gathered together in Paradise."
"1322","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he heard Arfajah, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be discords and discords, so whoever wants to divide the affair of this nation while it is united, strike his head with the sword, whoever he may be."
"1323","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn al-Minhal, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command fasting the white days and would say: They are the fasting of a lifetime."
"1324","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his grandfather, that he circumambulated with Muadh ibn Afra around the House after Asr - or after Fajr - and did not pray, so I said: Will you not pray? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises."
"1325","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Thalabah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, from his uncle Mujammi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Mary will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."
"1326","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Talhah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"1327","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi, that he gifted game meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in pilgrim sanctity, so he returned it, and he saw displeasure on his face, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not a rejection of you, but we are in pilgrim sanctity."
"1328","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no reserved sanctuary except for Allah and His Messenger."
"1329","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maiz al-Amiri, from Sufyan ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a matter I may hold fast to! He said: Say: I believe in Allah, then be steadfast. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you fear most for me? He said: So he pointed with his hand to his own tongue."
"1330","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and al-Masudi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I heard Usamah ibn Sharik saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his Companions were as if birds were upon their heads, and the Bedouins came to him from all sides and asked him about things in which there is no harm, saying: O Messenger of Allah, is there sin upon us in such-and-such, is there sin upon us in such-and-such! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Servants of Allah, Allah has removed hardship - or he said: Allah has lifted hardship - except for a man who wrongs another man in his honor; that is what brings sin and ruin. And they asked him about medicine, so he said: Servants of Allah, treat yourselves, for Allah Almighty has not placed a disease except that He has placed for it a cure, except for one disease: old age. And Usamah had grown old, so he said: So do you see any cure for me?!"
"1331","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and al-Masudi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the best of what people have been given? He said: Good character."
"1332","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Masud ibn Niyar, he said: Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah came to our gathering and narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you estimate the crop, leave a third; if you do not leave a third, then leave a fourth."
"1333","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Israil al-Jushami informed me, he said: I heard Jadah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a man was relating a dream to him, and he saw a stout man and began piercing his belly with something in his hand, saying: If some of this were elsewhere it would be better for you."
"1334","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Israil, from Jadah, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a man was brought to him, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this one wanted to kill you! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have not been frightened, you have not been frightened; had you intended that, Allah would not have given you power over killing me."
"1335","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nawfal ibn Muawiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever misses the prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken away."
"1336","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Shall I not guide you to the people of Paradise? Every weak, oppressed one; if he swears by Allah, Allah fulfills it for him. And he said: The people of the Fire are every coarse, insolent, arrogant one."
"1337","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, he heard Harithah ibn Wahb, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Give charity, for a time will soon come when a man walks with his charity and the one to whom he brings it says: Had you come to us yesterday I would have accepted it, but as for now I have no need of it! So he will find no one to accept it."
"1338","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzai saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer at Mina, while we were more numerous than we ever were and most secure, two rakahs."
"1339","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik al-Salimi, who said: I used to lead my people Banu Salim in prayer, and when the torrents came it was hard for me to cross a valley between me and the mosque, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it is hard for me to cross it; if you see fit to come to me and pray in my house in a spot I will take as a place of prayer! He said: I will do so. So he came to me the next day, and I detained him for a meal of khazirah, and when he entered he did not sit until he said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? So I pointed to the spot where I pray, and he prayed two rakahs. Then some men of the Ansar heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, so they began coming until they were many. Then a man of the household said: What has Malik ibn al-Dukhshum done? Then a man of the household said: That is a hypocrite who does not love Allah and His Messenger! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not say: There is no god but Allah? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best; as for us, we see no affection or talk of his except toward the hypocrites! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has forbidden the Fire for whoever says: There is no god but Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah. Mahmud said: Then I narrated this hadith in a gathering in which Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was present in the land of the Romans during the expedition of Yazid ibn Muawiyah, and Abu Ayyub objected to me, saying: I do not think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever said this. Mahmud said: So I vowed that if Allah returned me in well-being I would ask Itban ibn Malik about this hadith in his peoples mosque if he were alive. So I entered ihram for Umrah from Iliya, then came to Madinah and found Itban an elderly blind man leading his people in prayer. I stated my lineage to him and he recognized me - or he said: I asked him about this hadith. He said: So he narrated to me as he had narrated to me the first time. Al-Zuhri said: And we consider that was before the revelation of the binding ordinances, for a matter has come down; we found the scholars holding that view. Whoever of you can avoid being deluded, let him not be deluded; we fear the matter may have come to this: Allah Almighty imposed upon the people of this word duties, and we fear the matter may have come to them."
"1340","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, that he remembered a mouthful of water the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spewed in their house."
"1341","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Jawn ibn Qatadah, from Salamah ibn al-Muhabbaq al-Hudhali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tanning the hide is its slaughtering."
"1342","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Murrah narrating from Abu Sad al-Zuraqi, that a man of Ashja asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about withdrawal, and he said: Whatever is decreed in the womb will be."
"1343","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Urwah ibn al-Jad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"1344","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Hadid narrating from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings. He said: And whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition he sent it at the beginning of the day. And Sakhr was a merchant; he used to send his servants at the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased until he did not know where to put it."
"1345","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwai narrating from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the dawn prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf at Mina, and when he finished his prayer there were two men at the back of the mosque who had not prayed with the people, so the two were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while their limbs trembled, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevented you from praying with us? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our lodgings! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do so; when you have prayed in your lodgings then come to the imam while he is praying, pray with him, for it will be voluntary for you."
"1346","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad narrating from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque of al-Khayf, and I took his hand, and it was more fragrant than the scent of musk and cooler than snow."
"1347","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, both from Said al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah al-Azdi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the shade of a large tree with a scribe dictating to him, and he said: O Ibn Hawalah, shall I not write you down? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me! He kept dictating and dictating, and I looked and there were the names of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, so I knew they would only be recorded for good. He said to me: O Ibn Hawalah, shall I not write you down? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! Then he said: O Ibn Hawalah, how will you be when a tribulation arises in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. Then he said: O Ibn Hawalah, how will you be when another arises, the one before it like the snort of a rabbit, as if they were the horns of cows? I said: Whatever Allah and His Messenger choose for me. And a veiled man passed, and he said: This one and his companions on that day are upon the truth! So I went to him and took him by the shoulder and turned his face toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This one. And it was Uthman ibn Affan."
"1348","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Hawalah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: You will come upon a man wrapped in a cloak of the people of Paradise, pledging allegiance with the people. He said: So we came upon Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, wrapped in a cloak, pledging allegiance with the people."
"1349","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Burzin narrated to us, he said: Sayyar ibn Salamah al-Riyahi - of Banu Tamim - narrated to us, from al-Bara al-Saliti of Banu Abs, from Nuqadah al-Asadi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to a man to ask him for a mount on one of his she-camels, but he refused, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he sent him to another man to ask him for a mount, and he sent him a she-camel, so Nuqadah came leading it, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it he said: May Allah bless it and whoever sent it. Nuqadah said: O Messenger of Allah, and whoever brought it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And whoever brought it. So it was brought forward to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and milked and gave abundantly, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, increase the wealth and children of so-and-so - the first one who refused - and said to the owner of the she-camel: O Allah, make the provision of so-and-so day by day."
"1350","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, he said: I heard Abu Hajib narrating from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing ablution from the leftover ablution water of a woman. Thus Abu Dawud narrated to us. And Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith said: From Shubah, from Asim, from Abu Hajib, from al-Hakam ibn Amr."
"1351","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands when he began the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"1352","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks."
"1353","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cutting meat from the shoulder of a sheep, then he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"1354","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and al-Masudi narrated to us, they said: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah informed us, he said: I heard Qutbah ibn Malik saying: I prayed the dawn prayer behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited Qaf; he recited: {And tall palm trees}. Al-Masudi said in his hadith: When he recited {And tall palm trees} I said to myself: What is their tallness?"
"1355","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, he said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Hilal narrating from a man of Banu Thalabah ibn Yarbu, that some people of them came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Banu Thalabah had killed a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - so a man said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Thalabah ibn Yarbu killed so-and-so! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No soul commits a crime against another. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned charity, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is the giving hand; your mother and your father, and your sister and your brother, then the nearest then the nearest. Thus Shubah said: From a man of Banu Thalabah; and al-Thawri said: From Thalabah ibn Zahdam."
"1356","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah, from his grandfather Arfajah ibn Asad, that his nose was injured on the day of al-Kulab in the pre-Islamic period, so he took a nose of silver, but it rotted upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take a nose of gold."
"1357","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed under a blind banner, supporting tribal partisanship and angered for tribal partisanship, his death is one of ignorance."
"1358","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrating from Hakim ibn Qays ibn Asim, that his father instructed in his will, saying: When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not wailed over."
"1359","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim, he said: I heard Hafsah bint Sirin narrating from al-Rabab, from Salman ibn Amir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fasts, let him break his fast with dates; if he does not find them, then with water, for it is pure."
"1360","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi, from Muawiyah al-Laythi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People wake up suffering drought, then Allah brings them provision from Him, then they wake up as polytheists, saying: We were given rain by such-and-such star."
"1361","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir said to me: What is your name? I said: Shubah. He said: Abu Shubah narrated to me - and he was gentle - from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, who said: A man slapped his servant boy - or a person - so Suwayd said: Did you not know that the face is inviolable? I saw myself as the seventh of seven brothers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no servant for us but one, then one of us slapped him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to free him."
"1362","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, I heard Hilal al-Mazini saying: I heard Suwayd ibn Muqarrin saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a jar in which drink had been steeped, and I asked him about that, so he forbade me, and I broke the jar."
"1363","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a man, from Hanzalah al-Ansari, that a man greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he did not return it until he wiped himself with dust, saying: Nothing prevented me from returning it to you except that I was not in ablution - or he said: He did not return it to him until he wiped himself with dust, then returned it to him."
"1364","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Hafs ibn Asim narrating from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque while I was praying, and he called me, so I prayed then came, and he said: What prevented you from answering me when I called you? Have you not heard Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saying: {O you who believe, respond to Allah and the Messenger when he calls you to what gives you life}? I shall surely teach you the greatest chapter in the Quran before I leave the mosque. He said: So I walked with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we were about to reach the door of the mosque, and I said: He forgot! So I reminded him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, you said to me such-and-such! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds} - the seven oft-repeated and the Great Quran which I have been given."
"1365","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr al-Saksaki narrated to us, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Mulayki, from Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami - and he had companionship - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slain are three: a believing man who went out with himself and his wealth, met the enemy and fought until he was killed; that is the tested one in the tent of Allah beneath His Throne, whom none surpass except the Prophets by the degree of Prophethood. And a believing man who had burdened himself with sins and wrongs, met the enemy and fought until he was killed; that is a cleansing that wiped away his sins and wrongs; the sword indeed erases wrongs. And it will be said to him: Enter through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish, for they are eight gates, and Hell has seven gates, some better than others. And a hypocritical man who went out with himself and his wealth and fought until he was killed; that one is in the Fire, for the sword does not erase hypocrisy."
"1366","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from al-Hakam or Abu al-Hakam - a man of Thaqif - from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and sprinkled his private part."
"1367","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Zaidah narrated to us, from Husayn, he said: Umarah ibn Ruwaybah - and he had companionship - saw Bishr ibn Marwan raising his hands in supplication - meaning on Friday. Shubah said: So he reviled him or belittled him; and Zaidah said: May Allah disfigure these two hands; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did no more than this. And Abu Dawud pointed with the forefinger."
"1368","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Amr ibn al-Sharid al-Thaqafi, from his father, that a leper came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell him to go back, for I have pledged allegiance with him."
"1369","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala al-Taifi narrated to us, he said: And Amr ibn al-Sharid narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite a hundred rhyming verses of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt; whenever I recited a verse to him he said: More. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He almost embraced Islam in his poetry."
"1370","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has more right to his adjoining property. He said: So I said to Amr: What is his saqab? He said: His preemption."
"1371","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas, from Abd Allah ibn Utbah, who said: Ibn Masud was asked about a woman whose husband died without consummating with her and without assigning her a dower, and he refused to say anything about it, then he was asked about it after a month, and he said: I say concerning it: O Allah, if it is correct it is from You, and if it is wrong it is from me; she gets the dower of one of her womenfolk, she gets inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period. Then a man of Ashja stood and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged among us likewise concerning Barwa bint Washiq. So he said: Bring two witnesses to this! So Abu Sinan and al-Jarrah bore witness; two men of Ashja."
"1372","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: He wrote to me, and I read it to him, and he said to me: When I write to you I have narrated to you. He said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Salamah ibn Qays al-Ashjai, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you perform ablution, blow out your nose, and when you cleanse with stones, make it odd."
"1373","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah, Warqa, Sallam, and Qays narrated to us, all from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Tariq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you are in prayer, do not spit toward your face nor to your right, but spit toward your left if it is empty, otherwise beneath your foot. And Qays said: The left."
"1374","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Khalid ibn Umayr, who said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed us and said in his sermon: Indeed I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no food for nearly a month except tree leaves, until our mouth corners were ulcerated from it."
"1375","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, saying: Before the Hour there will be liars. Then he said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: What did he say? He said: Beware of them."
"1376","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, saying: Islam will not cease to be mighty until twelve caliphs. Then he said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: What did he say? He said: All of them are of Quraysh."
"1377","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Sulami, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and my mother spread a woolen garment for him and he sat upon it, then she brought him dates and he began eating and throwing the stones thus - and Abu Dawud twisted his two fingers, the forefinger and the middle - as one throws the stone above his finger. Then drink was called for and he drank, then gave to the one on his right. Then my mother said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for us! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for them what You have provided them, forgive them and have mercy on them."
"1378","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I raided in the caliphate of Abu Bakr in the expeditions and otherwise."
"1379","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mukhariq, he said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab saying: The delegation of Bajilah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Begin with the Ahmasians, and he supplicated for us."
"1380","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Lam, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Muzdalifah and said: Have I any Hajj? So he said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer and stood with us at this standing-place until he pours forth, having poured forth before that from Arafat by night or day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his rites."
"1381","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadh-dha, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ibn Abi al-Jada, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People more numerous than Banu Tamim will surely enter Paradise through the intercession of a man of my nation."
"1382","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, who said: I was among the captives of Qurayzah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that whoever had grown pubic hair be killed, so I was among those who had not grown it, and I was spared."
"1383","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Rifaah ibn Shaddad, he said: Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man grants a man safety for his life then kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the slain one was a disbeliever."
"1384","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rifaah ibn Shaddad, who said: I was the most intimate with al-Mukhtar - meaning the liar. One day I entered upon him and he said: You entered after Gabriel just rose from this chair. So I reached for the hilt of my sword and said: What am I waiting for, to walk between the head of this one and his body, until I remembered a hadith Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man grants a man safety for his blood then kills him, a banner of treachery will be raised for him on the Day of Resurrection. So I restrained myself from him."
"1385","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Imran, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not complete the takbir."
"1386","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Jami ibn Shaddad informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, who said: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah, and they mentioned a man who died of a stomach ailment and wanted to attend his funeral, so one of them said to the other: Did he not say - or did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He whom his belly kills will never be punished in his grave? So the other said: Yes indeed."
"1387","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Surad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Confederates: Now we will raid them and they will not raid us."
"1388","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Kurz ibn Alqamah, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have a duration or an end it reaches? He said: Yes; by Allah, there is no household of Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good except that He brings Islam to them. He said: Then what? He said: Then tribulations fall like darkness. So the man said: Never, if Allah wills. So he said: Yes indeed; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will return as black serpents pouring forth, striking one anothers necks."
"1389","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Rifaah ibn Arabah al-Juhani, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at al-Kadid - or he said: at Qudayd - some men of us began asking permission to go to their families, and he permitted them, then he praised Allah and spoke good, then said: What is the matter that the side of the tree nearer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more hateful to you than the other side? Then none of the people was seen except weeping. Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, he who asks your permission after this is indeed a fool. So he praised Allah and spoke good, and said: I testify before Allah that no servant dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah truthfully from his heart, then remains upright, except that he will be led into Paradise. And he said: My Lord has promised me to admit into Paradise of my nation seventy thousand with no reckoning upon them and no punishment, and I indeed hope they will not enter it until you and those righteous among your spouses and offspring take dwellings in Paradise."
"1390","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Rifaah al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a third of the night has passed - or he said: two-thirds of the night - Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and says: I do not ask about My servants from anyone other than Me; who is the one seeking My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who is the one calling upon Me that I may answer him? Who is the one asking Me that I may give him? Until dawn breaks."
"1391","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym, who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was read to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: Do not benefit from carrion in anything, neither hide nor sinew."
"1392","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lost property of a Muslim is the kindling of the Fire."
"1393","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Raja, from Mihjan, who said: Mihjan took my hand until we reached the mosque of Basra, and there was Buraydah al-Aslami sitting at one of the doors of the mosque, and in the mosque was a man called Sukbah prolonging the prayer. And Buraydah had a jesting manner, so Buraydah said: O Mihjan, will you not pray as Sukbah prays? So Mihjan did not answer him anything, and Mihjan said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand until we ascended Uhud, and he looked over Madinah and said: Woe to it as a town, its people will leave it at its most flourishing; the Dajjal will come and find upon every one of its gates a drawn-sworded angel, so he will not enter it."
"1394","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Raja, from Mihjan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand until we reached the portico of the mosque, and there was a man bowing and prostrating and bowing and prostrating, so he said to me: Who is this? So I said: This is so-and-so, and I began praising him, saying: This, this! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not let him hear, lest you destroy him. Then he went with me until he reached the door of a chamber, then released his hand from mine, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your religion is its easiest - he said it three times."
"1395","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Shimr narrated to us, he said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat. He said: I said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1396","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon and saw my father in the sun, so he commanded him - or gestured to him - to come near to the shade."
"1397","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he heard Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to announce at Mina: None enters Paradise except a Muslim soul, and these are days of eating and drinking."
"1398","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi, that Abu Hadrad sought the help of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a marriage, so he said: How much have you given as dower? He said: Two hundred dirhams. He said: Had you been scooping from Buthan you would not have increased."
"1399","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from one who heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj al-Aslami, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what removes from me the blame of fosterage? He said: A detachment; a male slave or a female slave."
"1400","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you take the property of his companion in jest or earnest, and when one of you takes the staff of his companion let him return it to him. Abu Bishr said: Thus it is in my book from Abu Dawud, while people say: From Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abd Allah ibn al-Saib, from his father, from his grandfather."
"1401","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas saying: My father came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and sometimes he said: From his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he saw him of unkempt appearance, so he said: Do you have wealth? I said: Yes. He said: From what kind of wealth? I said: From all wealth; from camels, slaves, horses, and sheep. He said: When Allah gives you wealth, let its trace be seen upon you. Then he said: Are the camels of your family born with sound ears, then you deliberately take a knife and cut their ears, saying: These are Bahirah, and you slit them or slit their skins, saying: These are Sarum, forbidding them for yourself and your family? So all wealth Allah has given you is lawful for you. Shubah said: He sometimes says this and sometimes does not say it: And the knife of Allah is sharper than your knife, and the arm of Allah is stronger than your two arms - and sometimes he said: And the knife of Allah is sharper, and the arm of Allah is stronger."
"1402","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man - I stayed with him and he did not honor me, host me, or entertain me, then he stayed with me; shall I recompense him or entertain him? He said: Rather entertain him."
"1403","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Maqil narrating from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from people of Muzaynah al-Zahirah, that Abjar - or Ibn Abjar - asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth except my donkeys! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed your family from the fat of your wealth, for I only disliked for them the roaming beasts of the town."
"1404","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Yazid ibn Murrah, from Salamah ibn Yazid al-Jufi, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My mother died, and she used to honor the guest, feed the neighbor and the orphan, and she buried alive in the pre-Islamic period, and I have ample wealth; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam benefits only one who reaches it; she and what she buried are in the Fire. He said: He saw that it weighed upon me, so he said: And the mother of Muhammad is with her; there is no good in them both."
"1405","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Yazid ibn Murrah, from Salamah ibn Yazid al-Jufi, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying concerning the words of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Indeed, We have created them anew, and made them virgins, loving, of equal age}: Of the previously married and the unmarried."
"1406","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nahhaz ibn Judayy al-Jufi, from Sinan ibn Salamah, that he narrated to him from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered pots to be overturned, and in them were meats of domestic donkeys."
"1407","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar saying: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hajj is Arafah; Hajj is Arafat; whoever reaches Arafah before dawn breaks has reached Hajj, or his Hajj is complete."
"1408","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yamar saying: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The days of Mina are three days; whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him."
"1409","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Bishr ibn Hazn al-Nasri, who said: The owners of camels and sheep boasted before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dawud was sent while he was a shepherd of sheep, and Musa was sent while he was a shepherd of sheep, and I was sent while I shepherded sheep for my family at Jiyad."
"1410","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people to gain from one another, but when one of you consults his brother, let him advise him sincerely."
"1411","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, he said: My father asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast one day of the month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for me, increase for me! He said: Fast one day of the month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for me, increase for me! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast one day of the month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have strength, so increase for me! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast two days of the month. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have strength, so increase for me! Until I thought he would not increase him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast three days of the month."
"1412","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, who said: We came from the Romans, and when we neared Hims we said: If we passed by Wahshi and asked him about the killing of Hamzah. So we met a man and mentioned that to him, and he said: He is a man overcome by wine; if you find him sober, you will not ask him about anything except that he informs you, but if you find him drinking, do not ask him. So we went until we reached him; something had been spread for him at his door and he was sitting sober, and he said: Ibn al-Khiyar? I said: Yes; I have not seen you since your mother carried you to me at Dhu Tuwa when she laid you down and I saw your feet and recognized them. He said: I said: We came to ask you about the killing of Hamzah! So he said: I shall narrate to you as I narrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he asked me. I was a slave of the family of Mutim, and the son of the brother of Mutim said to me: If you kill Hamzah in revenge for my uncle, you are free! So I went on the day of Uhud with my spear, and I am a man of Abyssinia who plays with it as they play, and I went out that day intending to kill no one nor fight anyone except Hamzah. So I went out and there was Hamzah like a reddish-brown camel, none rose against him except that he struck him down with the sword, so I feared him. And a man of the sons of Siba hastened toward him, and I heard Hamzah saying: Come to me, O son of the cutter of clitorises! So he charged him and killed him. And I kept evading him, taking cover by a tree with my spear, until when I got my opportunity at him I shook the spear until I was satisfied with it, then threw it and it fell between his nipples; he tried to rise but could not, so I killed him, then I took my spear. I killed no one and fought no one else, and when I came to him I was freed. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came I wanted to flee from him toward Sham, then a man came to me and said: Woe to you, O Wahshi; by Allah, no one comes to Muhammad and testifies his testimony except that he leaves him alone! So I went, and he was aware of me only when I was standing at his head testifying the testimony of truth. He said: Are you Wahshi? I said: Yes, Wahshi. He said: Woe to you, narrate to me about the killing of Hamzah. So I began narrating to him as I narrated to you both. Then he said: Woe to you, O Wahshi, hide your face from me so that I do not see you. So I used to keep away from being seen by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah took His Prophet, peace be upon him. When there occurred of the affair of Musaylimah what occurred and the expedition was sent to him, I went out with it and took my spear. We met, and I and a man of the Ansar hastened toward him; your Lord knows best which of us killed him. If I killed him, then I have killed the best of people and the worst of people. Sulayman ibn Yasar said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I was in the army that day, and I heard a caller saying concerning Musaylimah: The black slave has killed him."
"1413","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {For those who do good is the best reward and more}. He said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, a caller will call: O people of Paradise, you have a promise with Allah! So they will say: And what is it? Has He not whitened our faces, made our scales heavy, and admitted us to Paradise? So it will be said to them that three times. He said: Then He, Blessed and Exalted, will manifest Himself to them and they will look upon Him, and that will be greater to them than all they were given."
"1414","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Salih Abu al-Khalil narrating from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not separated; if they are truthful and make clear, their sale will be blessed for them, but if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale will be wiped out."
"1415","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salih, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this."
"1416","Abu Dawud said: And Hammam said: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrating from Hakim ibn Hizam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this."
"1417","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and persisted in asking, so he said: What a strange question of yours, O Hakim! This wealth is sweet and green, the filth of peoples hands; and the Hand of Allah is the upper, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the receiver, and the lowest of hands is the hand of the receiver."
"1418","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abd Allah ibn Ismah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I buy sales; what of them is lawful for me and what is unlawful for me? So he said to me: When you sell a sale, do not sell it until you take possession of it."
"1419","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrating from his father, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a house, and I heard him saying: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"1420","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey on a rainy day, so he commanded a caller who called: Prayer in the lodgings."
"1421","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Zurarah narrating from Ubayy ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches his parents or one of them, then enters the Fire, may Allah cast him far."
"1422","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Zurarah narrating from a man of his people called Malik, or Abu Malik, or Ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever takes an orphan among Muslims to his food and drink until he is independent of him, Paradise becomes due for him certainly. And whoever reaches his parents or one of them, then enters the Fire, may Allah cast him far. And whichever Muslim frees a Muslim neck, it will be his ransom from the Fire."
"1423","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Yala ibn Munabbih, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man wearing a cloak with traces of saffron or yellow upon it, so he said: Remove it from you, and put in your Umrah what you put in your Hajj. Qatadah said: And I said to Ata: We used to hear that he said: Tear it. He said: This is corruption, and Allah does not love corruption."
"1424","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Yala ibn Munabbih - or Ibn Umayyah - who said: Two men fought and one bit the other, so he pulled his hand from his mouth and knocked out his front tooth, so he disputed with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: One of you bites his brother as the young camel bites, so he annulled it. Al-Hakam said: Do you know what he annulled it means? I said: He voided it? He said: Yes."
"1425","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from Abu Izzah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends to take the soul of a servant in a land, He makes for him a need in it."
"1426","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Qays - or Qays ibn Zayd - from Shurayh, judge of the two cities, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will call the debtor on the Day of Resurrection and say: O son of Adam, wherein did you waste the rights of people? Wherein did you squander their wealth? So he will say: O Lord, I did not corrupt it, but I was afflicted either by drowning or by burning. So He, Almighty, will say: I am the most entitled to settle on your behalf today. Then his good deeds will outweigh his evil deeds, and he will be ordered to Paradise."
"1427","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Harun ibn Riab al-Usaydi, from Kinanah ibn Nuaym al-Adawi, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq al-Hilali, who said: I took upon myself a debt of reconciliation, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him concerning it, so he said: Stay, O Qabisah, until charity comes to us and we order for you from it. Then he said: O Qabisah, asking is not lawful except for one of three: a man who took upon himself a debt of reconciliation and asks concerning it until he obtains it, then refrains; and a man struck by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, so he asks until he obtains sufficiency of livelihood - or he said: support of livelihood - then refrains; and a man struck by severe need, and three men of sound judgment from his people stand and say: So-and-so has been struck by poverty or severe need, so he asks until he obtains sufficiency of livelihood - or support of livelihood - then refrains. And whatever besides them of asking is unlawful wealth its owner eats as unlawful wealth - he said it two or three times."
"1428","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, who said: I said to my father: O father, have you not prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar? He said: Yes. So I said: Did they supplicate the qunut in Fajr? He said: O my son, it is an innovation."
"1429","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu Hazim al-Ghifari, he said: My master Abu Ruhm narrated to me, who said: I attended Hunayn, I and my brother, with two horses with us, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted for us four shares, for me and my brother two shares each, and we sold two shares of Hunayn for two young camels."
"1430","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has raided, and whoever takes his place among his family has raided."
"1431","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution well then prays two rakahs without being inattentive in them will be forgiven."
"1432","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge concerning one who fornicated without being married: a hundred lashes and banishment for a year."
"1433","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib and Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, and from Abu Hurayrah, they said: Two men disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so one of them said: I adjure you by Allah to judge between us by the Book of Allah. Then his opponent stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired laborer for this one - meaning a worker - and he fornicated with his wife, so I ransomed him from him with a hundred sheep and a servant. When I asked the people of knowledge they informed me that upon my son is a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and upon the wife of this one is stoning! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall surely judge between you by the Book of Allah; as for the hundred sheep and the servant, they are returned to you, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and banishment for a year. And go in the morning, O Unays, to the wife of this one; if she confesses, stone her. So he went to her in the morning and asked her and she confessed, so he stoned her."
"1434","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, and from Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you fornicates, let him lash her; if she returns, let him lash her; if she returns, let him lash her; if she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope."
"1435","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to the market; had we shot arrows we would have seen where they landed."
"1436","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hani ibn Urwah ibn Qias narrated to us, from Abu Hudhayfah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Alqamah Abu Alqamah al-Thaqafi, that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gifted him a gift, so he said: Is it charity or a gift? For charity is sought thereby the Face of Allah, while a gift is sought thereby the face of the Messenger and the fulfillment of a need. So they asked him, and they kept asking him until they prayed Zuhr only with Asr."
"1437","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Uqbah ibn al-Harith, who said: I married the daughter of Abi Ihab in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a black slave-girl came and mentioned that she had suckled us both, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, she is lying! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How, when it has been said? Then I returned to him a second time and he said the like of that, then I returned to him a third time and he said: Leave her from you."
"1438","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ayman ibn Nabil al-Makki narrated to us, he said: I heard Qudamah ibn Abd Allah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the pillar on the day of Sacrifice upon a reddish she-camel, with no beating, no driving, and no crying out: Away, away."
"1439","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: We were with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Abd Allah ibn Takhfah al-Ghifari came, and Abu Salamah said to him: Narrate to us the hadith of your father! So he said: Yes; my father narrated to me that guests became many with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a man would take the hand of his guest, and a man would take the hand of his guest, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with us to his lodging and said: O Aisha, do you have anything? She said: Yes; a dish of dates and cheese I made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then bring it. So it was brought, and we ate until we paid no attention to it! Then he said: O Aisha, do you have a drink to give us? She said: O Messenger of Allah, a little milk for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she brought it to us and we drank until we paid no attention to it! Then we slept, and when it was morning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began waking us, and thus he used to do. He said: He came to me while I was sleeping upon my face and said: Who is this? So I said: It is I, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a lying posture Allah Almighty dislikes."
"1440","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe; he whose neighbor is not safe from his harms. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his harms? He said: His evil."
"1441","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Kathir al-Makki, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a delegate of my people, and I asked him about ablution, so he said: When you perform ablution, run water between the fingers and exaggerate in sniffing water unless you are fasting, and do not strike your wife as you strike your slave-girl."
"1442","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him draw near to his direction of prayer, so that Satan does not interrupt his prayer."
"1443","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not of righteousness to fast while traveling."
"1444","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Hafs ibn Asim narrating from Ibn Buhaynah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying the two rakahs of Fajr while the prayer had been established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dawn four! The dawn four!"
"1445","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Hanzalah al-Usaydi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you been as you are with me, the angels would have shaded you with their wings."
"1446","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duwali, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hunayn while we were new in disbelief, and we passed by a tree upon which the polytheists hung their weapons, called Dhat Anwat, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, make for us a Dhat Anwat as they have a Dhat Anwat! So he said: Allah is Greatest, you have said as the people of the Book said to Musa, peace be upon him: {Make for us a god as they have gods}. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely follow the ways of those before you."
"1447","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, and the time of prayer came, the Zuhr prayer, while over the cavalry of the polytheists was Khalid ibn al-Walid. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with his Companions, and the polytheists said: They have a prayer after this dearer to them than their sons, wealth, and selves - meaning the Asr prayer. So Gabriel, peace be upon him, descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between Zuhr and Asr and informed him, and this verse was revealed: {And when you are among them and lead for them the prayer} the verse to its end. When Asr came the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lined his Companions in two rows with their weapons upon them, and he magnified Allah, with the enemy before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they all magnified and all bowed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he stood for the second rakah and the others prostrated, then these advanced to the positions of those and those retreated to the positions of these, and he prayed with them another rakah and they all bowed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When they finished, these prostrated, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salutation. Abu Ayyash said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed this prayer twice; once at Usfan and once in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"1448","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, that Abu Basrah met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming, and said: From where have you come? He said: I have come from al-Tur; I prayed in it. He said: Had I met you, you would not have gone; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"1449","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, he said: I heard Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah narrating from Umm Salamah, from Abu Salamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant afflicted with an affliction who says: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; O Allah, with You I seek the reward of my affliction, so reward me in it and grant me better than it - except that Allah gives him that. She said: When Abu Salamah died I said: O Allah, reward me in my affliction, and I wanted to say: And grant me better than it, but I said: Who is better than Abu Salamah? Then I said it, and I hope Allah rewarded me in my affliction and I was granted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in return."
"1450","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: And I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, thereby and excellent, and whoever bathes, bathing is better."
"1451","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better, then let him expiate for his oath."""
"1452","Yasar al-Ansari. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jisr ibn Farqad narrated to us, saying: Salit ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar narrated to us, saying: ""My grandfather pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1453","Ubadah ibn Qurs. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurrah and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah al-Adawi, from Ubadah ibn Qurs - and Sulayman said: Ibn Qurt, and he was a Companion - who said: ""By Allah, you do deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the destructive sins."""
"1454","Abu Mahdhurah Samurah ibn Mi'yar. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Makhul, from Ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the adhan as nineteen phrases."" Abu Bishr said: And they mentioned that it is from Makhul, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father."
"1455","Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, saying: I heard Anas narrating from Abu Usayd al-Ansari that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best quarters of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj and Banu Sa'idah, and in all the quarters of the Ansar there is good."" He said: It was said: He has given them preference over us? He said: It was said: He has given you preference over many."
"1456","Attab ibn Asid. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abi Aqrab, from Attab ibn Asid, who said: ""I gained nothing from the office to which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed me except two ornamented cloaks which I gave to my freedman Kaysan to wear."""
"1457","Wathilah ibn al-Asqa'. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Abu Sa'd al-Shami narrated to me, saying: I saw Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' - and he was a Companion - praying in the mosque of Damascus wearing sandals, and he spat under his left foot then rubbed it into the ground. When he had prayed I said: Do you do this while you are one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"1458","Umar ibn Abi Salamah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Wajzah, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Mention the name of Allah - meaning over food - and eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."""
"1459","Hakim ibn Hizam. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Iyas informed me, saying: I heard Yusuf ibn Mahak narrating from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man seeks from me a sale which I do not have; shall I buy it for him? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not sell what you do not have."""
"1460","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, saying: I heard Yusuf ibn Mahak narrating from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: ""I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I would not fall down except while standing."" [literal; wording obscure]"
"1461","Kudayr al-Dabbi. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Kudayr al-Dabbi - Abu Ishaq said: And I heard it from him fifty years ago. Shu'bah said: And I heard it from Abu Ishaq forty or more years ago. Abu Dawud said: And I heard it from Shu'bah forty-five or forty-six years ago. Abu Bishr said: And I heard it from Abu Dawud more than fifty years ago. Abu Muhammad said: And I heard it from Yunus seventy years ago. The shaykh Abu Nu'aym said: I heard it seventy-six years ago - who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise! He said: ""Speak justly and give what is surplus."" He said: If I cannot do that? He said: ""Then feed food and spread peace."" He said: If I cannot do that or am unable? He said: ""Do you have any camels?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""Then look at a camel from your camels and a waterskin, and look for a household who drink water only every other day, and give them water to drink, for perhaps your camel will not perish nor your waterskin tear before Paradise becomes due for you."""
"1462","The uncle of Kharijah ibn al-Salt. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, from his uncle, that they came from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and passed by a tribe of Arabs, who said: Have you come from this Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes. He said: Is there a reciter of incantations among you? They said: Yes. He said: A man in fetters was brought, and a man of the people recited over him the Mother of the Qur'an three times in the morning and the evening, and something was ordered for them, but they said: No, until we ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the man asked him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Eat, for by my life, whoever eats by a false incantation, you have eaten by a true incantation."""
"1463","Amr ibn Salamah al-Jarmi. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Habib al-Jarmi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Salamah al-Jarmi narrated to us that his father and a group of his people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who will pray for us - or: who will lead us in prayer? He said: ""The one among you who has taken the most Qur'an will pray for you - or: will lead you."" He said: They returned and did not find anyone with more Qur'an than I had, so they put me forward, and I led them in prayer while I was a boy wearing a small cloak of mine. Mis'ar said: I found him leading them in prayer and praying over their funerals with no one disputing him until he passed away."
"1464","Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to me, from his father, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came upon Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri while he was bargaining over a cloak in the market, and said: What are you doing, O Amr? He said: I am buying this to give it in charity. He said to him: Then that is you. He said: Then he went on, then returned and said: O Amr, what did the cloak do? He said: I bought it and gave it in charity. He said: To whom? He said: To Ruqayqah. He said: And who is Ruqayqah? He said: My wife. He said: And you gave it in charity to your wife? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whatever you give them of anything, it is charity for you."" He said: O Amr, do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: By Allah, I will not leave you until you come to Aishah and ask her! He said: They went until they entered upon Aishah, and Amr said to her: O my mother, this Umar says to me: Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whatever you give them of anything, it is charity for you""? She said: O Allah, yes; O Allah, yes."
"1465","Uthman ibn Talhah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Uthman ibn Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Ka'bah."
"1466","Al-Muttalib. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Abi Anas, from Abdullah ibn Nafi' ibn al-Amya', from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Muttalib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Prayer is two by two, and you recite the tashahhud in every two rak'ahs, and humble yourself, and show your need, and raise your hands and say: O Allah, O Allah! Whoever does not do that, it is deficient; it is deficient."""
"1467","Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: While Ibn al-Zubayr was addressing us he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque exceeds by a hundred."" Ata said: As if it were a hundred thousand. He said: I said: O Abu Muhammad, is this virtue you mention for the Sacred Mosque alone or for the Haram? He said: No, rather for the Haram, for the whole Haram is a mosque."
"1468","Abu Juhayfah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this part of him white - and he pointed to the tuft below the lower lip."" He said: It was said to him: Whose like were you at that time, O Abu Juhayfah? He said: I used to trim arrows and feather them."
"1469","Abu Burdah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Burdah - and he is not the son of Abu Musa - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Drink but do not become intoxicated."""
"1470","Udhaynah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath."""
"1471","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Fihri. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Abdullah ibn Yasar - whose kunyah is Abu Hammam - from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Fihri, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Hunayn, and we marched on a very hot scorching day, and we alighted under the shade of trees. When the sun had passed its zenith I put on my armor and mounted my horse and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in his tent, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; the time to move has come, O Messenger of Allah! He said: ""Yes."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Bilal!"" He sprang up from beneath a lote tree as if his shadow were the shadow of a bird, and said: At your service and your aid, and may I be your ransom. He said: ""Saddle my horse for me."" He brought him two saddle pads of palm fiber with neither pride nor arrogance in them. He said: He mounted his horse, then we marched that day of ours, and we met the enemy and the two horsemen faced each other, and we fought them, and the Muslims turned away fleeing as Allah the Exalted said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: ""O servants of Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; O people, to me! I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted from his horse, and one who was nearer to him than I informed me that he took a handful of dust and threw it in the faces of the people and said: ""May the faces be deformed."" Ya'la ibn Ata said: Their sons informed us from their fathers that they said: None of us remained but his eyes and mouth were filled with dust, and we heard a clatter from the sky like iron passing over a new brass basin, and He defeated them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the spoils among the Muslims."
"1472","Rifa'ah al-Badri. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ja'far al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ali ibn Khallad narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Rifa'ah al-Badri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque - Rifa'ah said: And we were with him - when a man like a bedouin came, entered the mosque, prayed and made his prayer brief, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And upon you; repeat your prayer, for you have not prayed."" That weighed heavily on the people, that whoever makes his prayer brief has not prayed. He did that two or three times, each time saying the same to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, show me and teach me, for I am a human who is right and wrong. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution as Allah has commanded you, then say the takbir. If you have Qur'an with you, recite it, and if you have no Qur'an with you, praise Allah and declare His oneness and His greatness. When you bow, bow until you are tranquil, then raise your head and stand straight, then prostrate and be steady in prostration, then raise your head and sit straight, until you complete your prayer. If you do that, your prayer is complete, and if you fall short in any of that, you have only fallen short in your prayer."" This was easier for the people: that whoever falls short, falls short in his prayer and it is not all gone."
"1473","Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from her father. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Firas ibn Yahya, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the illness in which he died, none of us leaving, when Fatimah came walking, her gait differing in nothing from the gait of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he saw her he said: ""Welcome to my daughter,"" and seated her to his right - or to his left - then told her something in secret and she wept. I said to her, apart from his other wives: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) singled you out from among us with a secret and you weep? Then he told her something in secret and she laughed. He said: I said to her: I adjure you by my right - or by what right I have over you - tell me. She said: I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away I asked her, and she said: As for now, yes. As for my weeping, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Jibril, peace be upon him, used to review the Qur'an with me every year once, and he reviewed it with me this year twice, and I see my end has only drawn near,"" so I wept. He said to me: ""Fear Allah and be patient, for I am for you an excellent predecessor."" Then he said: ""O Fatimah, are you not pleased to be the chief of the women of the worlds"" - ""or the chief of the women of this nation"" - so I laughed."
"1474","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Fatimah said to me: ""O Anas, did your souls feel at ease pouring dust over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" Thabit said: And Fatimah said, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dying - or she said while he was heavy - : ""O my father, to Jibril we mourn him; O my father, how near to his Lord he is; O my father, the Gardens of Firdaws are his abode; O my father, he answered a Lord who called him."""
"1475","The musnad of Aishah, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her; what al-Aswad narrated from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would order one of us, when she was menstruating, to put on a garment, then he would fondle her."""
"1476","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds and varnished vessels."""
"1477","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as sheep, then nothing of him became forbidden."""
"1478","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, who heard Ibrahim narrating from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""I would look at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."""
"1479","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""I was in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and when I wanted to get up I would slip away stealthily."""
"1480","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Mansur and al-A'mash informed me, saying: I heard Ibrahim narrating from al-Aswad, who said: We were with Aishah when a tent fell upon a man and they laughed, so Aishah said: Do not mock; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""There is no Muslim who is pricked by a thorn or more, but Allah raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him by it."""
"1481","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that she wanted to buy Barirah for emancipation, but her owners wanted to stipulate her wala', so she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Buy her, for wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates."" He gave her the choice regarding her husband, and her husband was free. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and it was said: This is from what was given in charity to Barirah. He said: ""It is charity for her, and a gift for us."""
"1482","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, that Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: Tell me what the Mother of the Believers used to confide to you. Al-Aswad said: She informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Were it not that your people are recent in jahiliyyah, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and made two doors for it."" When Ibn al-Zubayr came to power he demolished it and made two doors for it."
"1483","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: I asked Aishah: How would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act in his house? She said: ""He would be in the service of his family, and when prayer came he would go out and pray."""
"1484","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a state of major impurity and wanted to sleep or eat, he would perform ablution."""
"1485","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."""
"1486","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard al-Aswad saying: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: ""He would sleep at the beginning of the night, and when it was the last part of the night he would pray witr, then come to his bed. If he had a need with his family he would attend to them, then sleep. When he heard the call - and perhaps she said: the adhan - he sprang up, and she did not say: he stood - if he was in a state of major impurity he would pour water over himself - and she did not say: he bathed - and if he was not in a state of major impurity he would perform ablution, then go out to prayer."""
"1487","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard al-Aswad and Masruq testifying about Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never came to me after Asr but he prayed two rak'ahs."""
"1488","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the insane until he recovers, and from the child until he understands."""
"1489","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would observe i'tikaf, and he would put his head out of the door of the mosque and I would wash it with lote-tree leaves while I was menstruating."""
"1490","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: A lizard was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not eat it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not feed it to the poor? He said: ""Do not feed them what you do not eat."""
"1491","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Hammad informed me, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, who said: I said to Aishah: What vessels did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid? She said: ""He forbade us gourds and varnished vessels."""
"1492","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not in a state of major impurity he would perform ablution, then pray two rak'ahs - meaning the two rak'ahs of Fajr - then go out to prayer."
"1493","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to enter ihram, he would anoint himself with the best perfume he could find, until I would see its glistening in his beard and head."""
"1494","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""I used to garland the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the garlanded animal would go out, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in a state of non-ihram, abstaining from none of his wives."""
"1495","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrating from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill of barley bread for two consecutive days until he passed away."""
"1496","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik and Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform ablution after bathing."
"1497","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not refrain from my face while fasting."" Meaning: he would kiss her."
"1498","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not leave a will."
"1499","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha', from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about al-Jadr - meaning al-Hijr - is it part of the House? He said: ""Yes."" She said: I said: What prevented them from including it in the House? He said: ""Your people lacked the funds."" She said: I said: Why did they make its door high? He said: ""Your people did that, to admit whom they wished and prevent whom they wished. Were it not that your people are recent in jahiliyyah, and I fear their hearts would deny it, I would have included what they left out, and brought its door down to the ground."""
"1500","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, that she said: ""It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."""
"1501","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted incantations for snake and scorpion stings."
"1502","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Ibrahim narrating from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: ""A woman could grant protection on behalf of the Muslims."""
"1503","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep while in a state of major impurity, not touching water."
"1504","Alqamah ibn Qays from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, who said: I asked Aishah: Would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) single out Friday night or Friday? She said: ""His deed was continuous, and which of you can do what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do?"""
"1505","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Alqamah and Shurayh ibn Arta'ah were with Aishah, and one of them said: Ask her about kissing for one fasting. One of them said: I would not speak obscenely in the presence of the Mother of the Believers. She said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting, and he was the most in control of his desire among you."""
"1506","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, saying: Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Alqamah, who said: We were with Aishah when Abu Hurayrah entered upon her, and she said: O Abu Hurayrah, are you the one who narrates that a woman was punished for a cat of hers, tying it up without feeding or watering it? Abu Hurayrah said: I heard it from him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Aishah said: Do you know what the woman was? He said: No. She said: The woman, along with what she did, was a disbeliever; the believer is too honored before Allah for Him to punish him for a cat. When you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), look at how you narrate."
"1507","Hammam ibn al-Harith from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Hammam ibn al-Harith was staying with Aishah and had a wet dream, and a slavegirl of Aishah saw him washing the trace of impurity from his garment and informed Aishah. Aishah sent to him: ""I remember that I would do no more than rub it off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1508","Masruq from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: ""When the last verses of Surat al-Baqarah were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque and recited them to the people, and he forbade trade in wine."""
"1509","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, who said: Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice and we chose him; was that a divorce?"""
"1510","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would visit a sick person he would wipe his face and chest - or he said: wipe over his chest - and say: ""Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness."" She said: When it was the illness in which he died, I began taking his hand to place it on his chest and saying these words, but he pulled his hand from my hand and said: ""O Allah, admit me to the Highest Companion."""
"1511","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah and Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with me one night, and I missed him and thought he had gone to one of his slavegirls, so I searched for him in the darkness of the night. Jarir said - and Shu'bah did not say it - she said: I reached him while he was prostrating, and I placed my hand on him, and I heard him saying: ""O Allah, forgive me what I concealed and what I revealed."""
"1512","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Masruq - or from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah - from Aishah, who said: A man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""What a bad servant of Allah and brother of the clan,"" then he entered upon him, and he turned to him with his face as if he held a rank with him. [literal; wording condensed]"
"1513","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha', from his father, from Masruq, who said: I asked Aishah about the practice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: ""The most beloved deed to him was the constant one."" I said: At what time would he rise? She said: ""When he heard the caller he would rise."" Abu Dawud said: Meaning the rooster."
"1514","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid and Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said: I asked Aishah about the word of Allah the Blessed and Exalted: {And he certainly saw him at the clear horizon} {And he certainly saw him at another descent}. She said: I am the first of this nation who asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: ""It is Jibril; I saw him twice: I saw him at the highest horizon, and I saw him at the clear horizon."""
"1515","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: ""We would eat the meat of the sacrifices after the tenth."""
"1516","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from his father, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved to begin with the right as much as he could,"" and she said once: ""In all his affairs: in his purification when he performed ablution, in putting on his sandals when he put them on, and in combing when he combed."""
"1517","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ash'ath, saying: I heard my father narrating from Masruq, who said: A Jewish woman came to Aishah asking her, and said to Aishah: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and Aishah asked him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The punishment of the grave is true."" Aishah said: After that I never heard him pray a prayer but he sought refuge in it from the punishment of the grave."
"1518","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ash'ath, saying: I heard my father narrating from Masruq, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while there was a man with her as if he disliked it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, he is my brother through breastfeeding. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Look at who your brothers are, for breastfeeding is only from hunger."" [i.e. only nursing in infancy counts]"
"1519","Al-Qasim from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with only Hajj in mind. When I was at Sarif I menstruated, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was weeping, and said to me: ""What makes you weep?"" I said: I have menstruated, and I wish I had not performed Hajj. He said: ""Glory be to Allah, it is only something Allah the Blessed and Exalted has decreed upon the daughters of Adam; perform all the rites, except do not circumambulate the House."" She said: When he came to Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: ""Whoever of you wishes may make it an umrah, except one who has a sacrificial animal with him."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered cows on behalf of his wives. When it was the night of departure I became pure, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, my companions return with Hajj and umrah, and I return with Hajj. He sent Ibn Abi Bakr with me, and I performed umrah from al-Tan'im."
"1520","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed me, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep before the night prayer, nor stay up after it."""
"1521","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss Uthman ibn Maz'un while he was dead."""
"1522","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to bathe from one vessel for major impurity."" Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah said: I like it because he said: for major impurity."
"1523","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, that she wanted to buy Barirah and emancipate her, while her owners wanted to stipulate wala', so Aishah mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Buy her and emancipate her, for wala' belongs only to the one who emancipates."" She said: Meat was brought, and he said: ""What is this?"" They said: Barirah gave it to us; it was given in charity to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is charity for her, and a gift for us."" He said: She was given the choice, and her husband was free. Shu'bah said: Then I asked him afterwards, and he said: I do not know whether he was free or a slave. Shu'bah said: I said to Simak ibn Harb: I am wary of asking him about the chain, so you ask him. He said: And he was harsh in character. Simak said to him after he had narrated: Did your father narrate this to you from Aishah? Abd al-Rahman said: Yes. When he left, Simak said to me: O Shu'bah, I have verified it for you from him."
"1524","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Aishah, who said: ""I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he exited ihram and when he entered ihram."""
"1525","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""A woman suffered prolonged bleeding at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was ordered - I said: Who ordered her, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I am not narrating to you anything from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - She said: So she was ordered to delay Zuhr and hasten Asr and bathe once for both, and delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and bathe once for both, and bathe for Fajr."""
"1526","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: ""I remember rubbing impurity off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without washing the spot."""
"1527","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to bathe from one vessel."""
"1528","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does in our matter what is not permissible, it is rejected."""
"1529","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray toward a spread garment over a small room of ours in which there were images, and he said: Keep this away from me."" Aishah said: So we made it into cushions."
"1530","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, who said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss Uthman ibn Maz'un while he was dead."" Abu Dawud said: Ash'ath ibn Sa'id said in this hadith with this chain: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that he wept until I saw tears flowing down his cheeks."
"1531","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Juwayriyah ibn Asma' narrated to us, from Nafi', that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed him, that Aishah informed him, who said: I bought a cushion with images on it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood at the door and did not enter, and I recognized displeasure on his face. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I repent to Allah the Mighty and Majestic - twice - what have I done? He said: ""What is this cushion?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought it for you to sit on and recline upon. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who make these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created. And the house in which such images - or such an image - are, the angels do not enter it."""
"1532","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Sumayyah, from Aishah. Abu Dawud said: A man of the people of Makkah also narrated it to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, who said: My father said to me: O my little daughter, what day is this? I said: ""This is Monday."" He said: On what day did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) die? I said: ""On Monday."""
"1533","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Talidan - of the family of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq - narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating from Aishah, who said: ""The most blessed marriage is the one with the least expense."" My father said to him: Did Aishah inform you of that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: This is how I was told it, and this is how I memorized it. [flag: chain stops at Aishah; not explicitly raised to the Prophet]"
"1534","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Talidan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Qasim narrating from Aishah, who said: ""The plague-stricken, the one with pleurisy, the woman in childbed, and the one with abdominal illness are martyrs."" My father said to him: Did Aishah narrate this to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: This is how she narrated to me, and this is how I memorized it. [flag: chain stops at Aishah; print notes name may be Isa ibn Maymun ibn Talidan]"
"1535","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, who said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of the night, and I thought he had gone to one of his wives, so I followed him and he ended up at al-Baqi', and said: ""Peace be upon you, O abode of believing people, and we shall join you, God willing. O Allah, do not deprive us of their reward, nor lead us astray after them."" Then he turned and saw me, and said: ""Woe to her, if only she could avoid doing what she did."" [literal]"
"1536","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Hand me the prayer mat."" She said: I am menstruating. He said: ""Your menstruation is not in your hand."" So I handed it to him."
"1537","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, saying: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating from Aishah, who said: ""I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his exiting ihram and for his entering ihram."""
"1538","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: {Verses precise, they are the Mother of the Book, and others allegorical} - the verse - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah the Mighty and Majestic has named them for you; when you see them, beware of them."" He said it three times."
"1539","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this verse {As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow} - the verse - and he said: ""Allah has named them for you; when you see them, beware of them."""
"1540","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that Abu Qu'ays sought permission to enter upon me. She said: I disliked giving him permission, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and I asked him about that. He said: ""Give him permission, for he is your uncle."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, how so, when only the woman breastfed me and the man did not breastfeed me! He said: ""Give him permission, for he is your uncle."" He said: Abu Qu'ays was the brother of Aflah, the husband of Aishah's wet nurse."
"1541","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought beads of onyx and divided them between the free woman and the slavegirl."
"1542","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed Duha as a regular practice, though I pray it."""
"1543","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband has nothing more than the fringe of a garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What do you want? Do you want to return to Rifa'ah? No, until you taste his little honey and he tastes yours."" [euphemism for consummation]"
"1544","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to bathe from one vessel; that cup was then called al-Faraq."""
"1545","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Zaynab bint Jahsh suffered prolonged bleeding for seven years, and she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered her to bathe and pray, and she would bathe for every prayer."
"1546","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Servants are the servants of Allah, and lands are the lands of Allah; whoever revives something dead of the land, it is his, and the unjust root has no right."""
"1547","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would avoid nothing."""
"1548","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Abyssinians would enter the mosque and play, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would shield me while I, a young girl, looked at them. Umar came and forbade them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave them, O Umar."" Then he said: ""They are the daughters of Arfidah."""
"1549","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""I would comb the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in i'tikaf, putting his head out to the threshold of the room's door, and I would comb him."""
"1550","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas said to his brother Sa'd: When you come to Makkah, take the son of the slavegirl of Zam'ah, for he is from me. When the day of the Conquest came, Sa'd came to him, and Abd ibn Zam'ah came and took his hand. Sa'd said: The son of my brother! He entrusted to me that he is his son. Abd ibn Zam'ah said: My brother, from my father's slavegirl, born on his bed. They disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother entrusted to me that when I come to Makkah I take the son of the slavegirl of Zam'ah, for he is his son. Abd ibn Zam'ah said: The son of my father's slavegirl, from my father's slavegirl, born on his bed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is yours, O Abd; the child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone. And veil yourself from him, O Sawdah bint Zam'ah,"" because of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw of his resemblance to Utbah. She never saw him until she met Allah."
"1551","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When dinner is served and prayer comes, begin with dinner."""
"1552","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the deceased dies, leave him."" [literal; leave off speaking ill of him]"
"1553","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Waqqas al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: My mother narrated to me that she entered upon Aishah."
"1554","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalah informed us of it, from al-Hasan, from Aishah, who said: A beggar woman entered upon me with her two sons, and I ordered three dates for her. She fed her two boys a date each and put a date in her mouth. The two boys ate their two dates, then looked at their mother, so she took the date out of her mouth and split it between them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, today I saw something wondrous. He said: ""And what is that?"" I informed him, and he said: ""Why do you wonder at a woman whom Allah has forgiven for her mercy to her child?"""
"1555","Abu Dawud said: Bahr al-Saqqa' said, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, and he mentioned similar to this hadith. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was weeping, and said: ""What makes you weep, O Aishah?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, the mother and her mercy - and I informed him - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is tried with any of them and treats them well, they will be a veil for him from the Fire."""
"1556","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A woman who had stolen was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: Who would dare approach him except his beloved Usamah? He came to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Usamah, do you know how the Children of Israel perished? When a noble among them stole he was not cut."" So he cut her hand. He said: She was a Makhzumi woman."
"1557","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with five, and said: ""We are a household; we pray witr with five."""
"1558","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Mu'ammal, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recline after the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"1559","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that ""a niche grave was dug for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1560","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Iyas ibn Dagfhal narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I was between him and the qiblah."""
"1561","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah and Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments, with neither shirt nor turban among them."""
"1562","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six - or seven - years old in Makkah, and consummated the marriage with me in Madinah when I was nine. Women came to me while I was a young girl with thick hair, playing on a swing, and they prepared me and presented me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1563","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""What a bad brother of the clan."" When he entered he was gentle with him. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you said such and such, then you were gentle with him! He said: ""O Aishah, the worst of people in rank before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people avoid - or: people leave - fearing his obscenity, or his evil."""
"1564","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, saying: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Aishah, who said: We used to say that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not die until he was given the choice between this world and the Hereafter. She said: When it was the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he died, hoarseness befell him, and I heard him saying: {With those upon whom Allah has bestowed favor, of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous} - the verse. Aishah said: So we knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was being given the choice."
"1565","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, saying: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I lay in front of him across."" Shu'bah said: Sa'd said: And I think she said: ""While I was menstruating."""
"1566","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, saying: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: Aishah said: What do you say interrupts prayer? He said: They said: The dog, the donkey, and the woman. Aishah said: The woman is then an evil beast; I remember lying across in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a funeral bier while he was praying."
"1567","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""Emigrant women would pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped in their woolen cloaks, unrecognized in the darkness of dawn."""
"1568","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""I performed tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning umrah - and I did not drive the sacrificial animal."""
"1569","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""A physiognomist entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Usamah ibn Zayd and Zayd were under a woolen cloak, their heads covered and their feet visible. The physiognomist said: These feet are part of one another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased with that and informed Aishah of it."""
"1570","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited me to race, and I raced him and beat him."""
"1571","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian, and any woman married without a guardian, her marriage is void, void, void. If she has no guardian, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."""
"1572","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Makhlad ibn Khufaf al-Ghifari, who said: I disputed before Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz concerning a slave who had been fraudulently sold to us, and we had taken some of his yield, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr was with him. Urwah narrated to him from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that produce belongs with liability for loss."
"1573","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Mujahid ibn Wardan, from Urwah, from Aishah, that a freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is there anyone here from the people of his village?"" They said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his inheritance."
"1574","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited aloud in the eclipse prayer."
"1575","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the cave of Hira, he came to Khadijah and said: ""Wrap me, wrap me,"" and he was wrapped. Then he said: ""O Khadijah, by Allah, I feared for myself."" Khadijah said to him: Rejoice, for by Allah, Allah will never disgrace you; you speak truthfully, maintain kinship, honor the guest, and help in the calamities of truth. Go; and she set out with him to Waraqah, an old blind man who read the Gospel in Hebrew. She said: O son of my uncle, listen to what the son of your brother says. Waraqah said to him: What do you say, O son of my brother? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him, and he said: By Allah, it is the Namus that was sent down upon Musa. Would that I were alive the day your people expel you, so I could aid you with strong aid. He said: ""And will my people expel me?"" He said: Yes; no one ever came with the like of what you have come with but he was opposed and harmed. Would that I were in it a young man."
"1576","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Burd Abu al-Ala', from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""I would open the door while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying; he would come facing the qiblah and open it for me, then return to his prayer."""
"1577","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, saying: Urwah informed me, from Aishah, who said: ""The first of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with was the true dream; he would see no dream in his sleep but it would come like the break of dawn, and solitude was made beloved to him. He would stay days in the cave of Hira worshipping, until the truth came to him suddenly one day while he was in the cave of Hira."""
"1578","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Aishah, that ""Sawdah gave her day to Aishah, for her place with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"1579","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, who said: ""Quraysh used to say: We are the residents of the House; we do not pour forth except from Mina, while the people would pour forth from Arafat. So Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent down: {Then pour forth from where the people pour forth}."""
"1580","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: ""Forty nights would pass upon us at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no lamp fire or other fire lit in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" He said: I said: On what would you live? She said: ""On the two black ones: dates and water."""
"1581","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b and Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Rifa'ah al-Qurazi divorced his wife with a final divorce, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr married her after him. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that he was unable to consummate with her, gesturing to the fringe of her cloak, and said: O Messenger of Allah, he has only like the fringe of a garment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled laughing, then said: ""You will not become lawful for him until he tastes your little honey."" [euphemism for consummation]"
"1582","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Aishah. Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe from major impurity, he would begin by washing his hands, then take with his right and pour upon his left, washing his private part until clean. Then he would rinse his mouth three times and sniff water three times, wash his face three times and his forearms three times each, then pour water over his head and body. When finished he would wash his feet."""
"1583","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ""would not fast any month of the year except Sha'ban, for he would fast all of Sha'ban."""
"1584","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me while fasting."""
"1585","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, who said: Aishah and Ibn Abbas informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ""stayed in Makkah ten years, with revelation coming down to him, and in Madinah ten years."""
"1586","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden."""
"1587","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, saying: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating, who said: Aishah was asked: Which deed was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: ""The most constant."""
"1588","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, or Abu Hurayrah - the doubt is not from Abu Dawud - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."""
"1589","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixed infusions."
"1590","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: ""The dawn never found him but sleeping"" - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1591","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, who said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: ""He would pray thirteen rak'ahs: pray eight, then pray witr, as if praying witr with nine, then pray two rak'ahs sitting. When he wanted to bow he would stand and bow, then pray two rak'ahs between the adhan and the iqamah"" - meaning of Fajr prayer."
"1592","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath."""
"1593","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, who said: I said to Aishah: Would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleep while in a state of major impurity? She said: ""Yes, and he would perform his ablution for prayer."""
"1594","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, saying: My uncle al-Harith narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed to the moon and said: ""Seek refuge in Allah from its evil, for it is the darkening night when it settles."""
"1595","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, one who heard Abu Salamah narrated to me, narrating from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his pure water until he pours over his hand three handfuls."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he woke would not do that until pouring over his hand three times. [literal; second clause obscure in print]"
"1596","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was in a gathering in which Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra were present, and they sent to A'isha asking: When does a pregnant woman complete her waiting period? She said: The husband of Subay'a bint al-Harith died while she was pregnant, and she gave birth three nights after his death, then she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded her to marry."
"1597","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Salt ibn Dinar Abu Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Uqba ibn Suhban al-Huna'i narrated to us, saying: I asked A'isha about the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: Then We caused to inherit the Book those We have chosen of Our servants, to the end of the verse, and she said to me: O my son, all of these are in Paradise. As for the foremost in good deeds, it is whoever passed away at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bore witness of life and provision; as for the moderate, it is whoever followed his example among his Companions until he joined him; and as for the wrongdoer to himself, it is the like of me and the like of you. He said: So she counted herself along with us."
"1598","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, saying: Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab narrated to us, saying: It was said to A'isha: Was poetry recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: It was the most hateful speech to him."
"1599","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Nawfal, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love the comprehensive supplications, and he would leave aside what was other than that."
"1600","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata narrating from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did all of that while traveling; he fasted and he broke his fast."
"1601","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Ata, from A'isha, who said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice, after he had stoned the jamra, before he circumambulated the House."
"1602","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Iyas ibn Abi Tamima narrated to us, from Ata, that a man was mentioned in the presence of A'isha and she cursed him - or reviled him - so it was said to her: He has died, and she said: I seek Allah's forgiveness for him. So it was said to her: O Mother of the Believers, you cursed him and then sought forgiveness for him! She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not mention your dead except with good."
"1603","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Ata, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O A'isha, indeed obscenity, had it been a man, would have been an evil man."
"1604","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Ata, from A'isha, who said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his bed one night, and I thought he had gone to one of his other wives, but I reached him while he was prostrating, and I heard him saying: Glory, Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit; the mercy of our Lord has preceded His wrath."
"1605","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fasted a complete month except Ramadan, nor stood an entire night in prayer until morning, nor recited the entire Qur'an in a single night."
"1606","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the two rak'as of Fajr: They are dearer to me than red camels."
"1607","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'isha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The one who recites the Qur'an while skilled in it shall be with the noble righteous scribes, and the one who recites the Qur'an - Hisham said: while it is hard upon him, and Shu'ba said: while it is difficult upon him - shall have two rewards."
"1608","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'isha, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adopted a practice, he loved to persist in it; and if illness or sleep overcame him, he would pray twelve rak'as during the day."
"1609","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara ibn Awfa, from Sa'd ibn Hisham, from A'isha, who said: A man named Shihab was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are Hisham."
"1610","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would become junub, then morning would come upon him, then he would bathe and fast, then he would go out to prayer, and I would hear his recitation."
"1611","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from his father, that he said: I entered upon A'isha, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake in the morning junub, then he would bathe, then he would go out early to the mosque with his head dripping, then he would fast that day."
"1612","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash semen from his garment, then he would go out while it still had spots upon it."
"1613","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Nafi' ibn Umar al-Jumahi and Rabah ibn Abi Ma'ruf narrated to us, both heard from Ibn Abi Mulayka, who said: I came to A'isha and mentioned to her what Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas reported from Umar, that the dead are punished by the weeping of their families over them. She said: By Allah, you inform me from one who is neither a liar nor accused, but hearing errs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never narrated to anyone that Allah punishes the believer by anyone's weeping; rather he said: The disbeliever's punishment is increased by his family's weeping over him, and in the Qur'an is what suffices you: No bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another."
"1614","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from A'isha, who said: I perfumed him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when he intended to enter ihram, with the best of my perfume that I could."
"1615","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Amir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from A'isha, that she menstruated, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Perform all the rites except circumambulating the House."
"1616","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me during the illness in which he died: Call Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr to me, that I may write a document for Abu Bakr over which there shall be no dispute after me. Then he said: Leave it, Allah forbid that the believers should dispute concerning Abu Bakr."
"1617","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Isma'il al-Suddi, from Abdullah al-Bahi, from A'isha, who said: I would not make up what was due upon me from Ramadan except in Sha'ban, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"1618","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah al-Bahi, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. She said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"1619","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir informed me, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never abandon four rak'as before Zuhr and two rak'as before the Fajr prayer."
"1620","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Khaythama narrating from Abu Atiyya al-Wadi'i, who said: Masruq and I entered upon A'isha, and we said: O Mother of the Believers, among us are two men from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them hastens breaking the fast and delays suhur, and the other delays breaking the fast and hastens suhur. She said: Which is the one who hastens breaking the fast and delays suhur? We said: Ibn Mas'ud. She said: That is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do."
"1621","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Khaythama narrating from Abu Atiyya al-Wadi'i, who said: I heard A'isha saying: By Allah, I know how the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. Then I heard her proclaiming the talbiya: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata lak."
"1622","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from A'isha, who said: I would drink from the vessel, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take it and place his mouth where my mouth had been, and I would gnaw the bone, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take it and place his mouth where my mouth had been."
"1623","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, who said: A'isha said to me: Whoever narrates to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated standing, do not believe him, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never urinated except sitting."
"1624","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from A'isha, that she was upon a camel and began turning it by striking it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O A'isha, be gentle, for it is never in anything except that it adorns it, and it is never removed from anything except that it disgraces it."
"1625","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yazid ibn Babanus, who said: We entered upon A'isha, and with us was a man who asked her, saying: O Mother of the Believers, what do you say concerning al-irak? She said: Menstruation? Then she said: O people of Iraq, will you not speak as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, spoke? Then she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would embrace me and take from my head while I was menstruating, with the waist-wrap upon me."
"1626","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Malih al-Hudhali, that some women from the people of Hims, or from the people of Sham, entered upon A'isha, and she said: Are you the ones whose women enter the bathhouses? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no woman who removes her clothes outside her husband's house except that she has torn the veil between her and Allah."
"1627","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abdullah ibn Abi Musa al-Nasri, who said: A'isha said to me: Do not abandon standing in prayer at night, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never abandoned it, and when he was ill - or she said: languid - he would pray sitting."
"1628","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Abu Ubaydallah al-Jadali saying: I asked A'isha, may Allah be pleased with her, about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He was not obscene, nor deliberately obscene, nor loud in the markets; he did not repay evil with evil, but he would pardon and overlook - or she said: pardon and forgive; Abu Dawud doubted."
"1629","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Maysara, who said: A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command one of us while menstruating to wrap her waist-cloth, then enter with him into his blanket."
"1630","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five vermin are killed in the non-sacred territory and in the sacred territory: the mouse, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the pied crow."
"1631","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"1632","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, saying: I heard Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Awf narrating from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned toward me to kiss me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I too am fasting, and he kissed her."
"1633","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from A'isha, that she used to take on debt, so it was said to her: O Mother of the Believers, what is with you and debt? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever intends to repay a debt, the help of Allah shall be with him, and I seek that help."
"1634","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Umara ibn Abi Hafsa, from Ikrima, who said: A'isha said: A trader arrived with goods, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would cast aside these two coarse garments of yours and send to such-and-such trader and he would sell you two garments on credit until ease. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent word: Send me two garments on credit until ease. He said: Muhammad wants to take my wealth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, they have certainly known that I am the most faithful of them to trusts, and the most fearing of them of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or words to that effect."
"1635","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', who heard Abu Qilaba, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, the foster-son of A'isha, from A'isha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no man over whom a community of people prays, all of them interceding for him, except that they are granted intercession for him."
"1636","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Warqa' narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a prayer and sleep overcomes him over it - or sleeps past it - Allah writes for him the reward of his prayer, and his sleep is a charity from Allah with which He has been charitable to him."
"1637","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abis ibn Rabi'a, who said: I came to A'isha and said: O Mother of the Believers, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the meat of sacrifices beyond three days? She said: No; few among them sacrificed, so he commanded that those who sacrificed feed those who had not sacrificed, and I remember we would store the trotters of the sacrifices and eat them after the tenth."
"1638","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Imran, from Talha ibn Abdullah, from A'isha, who said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, so to which of them shall I give a gift? He said: To the nearer of them to you in door."
"1639","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abbad, from A'isha, who said: When the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) occurred and they wanted to wash him, sleep fell upon them until the hand of each one of them was at his chin, and they were called to from the direction of the house: Wash him above his clothes. A'isha said: Had I known then what I know now, none but his wives would have washed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1640","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Thumama ibn Hazn, who said: I met A'isha and asked her about nabidh, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba', the muzaffat, the naqir, and the hantam. And she called an Abyssinian slave girl and said: Ask this one, for she used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I would make nabidh for him in a waterskin, then tie its mouth and hang it, and in the morning he would drink it."
"1641","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri informed me, from his father, that he entered upon A'isha and said to her: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whatever you have given them of anything, it is charity for you? She said: O Allah, yes; O Allah, yes."
"1642","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman, who said: A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me among those who, when they do good, rejoice, and when they do evil, seek forgiveness."
"1643","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays and Sallam narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss in the month of fasting. And Qays said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"1644","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Yazid al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Harim narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as in Makka - meaning the obligatory prayers. Then when he came to Madina, and four and three rak'as were obligated upon him, he prayed them, abandoning the two rak'as he used to pray in Makka, as a completion for the traveler."
"1645","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: A'isha said: I never saw anyone upon whom pain was more apparent than upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1646","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul: It was said to A'isha: Abu Hurayra says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in three: in the house, the woman, and the horse. So A'isha said: Abu Hurayra did not remember correctly, for he entered while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: May Allah destroy the Jews, they say: Ill omen is in three: in the house, the woman, and the horse. So he heard the end of the hadith and did not hear its beginning."
"1647","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Malik ibn Urfuta, from Abd Khayr, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba', the hantam, and the muzaffat."
"1648","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, saying: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed me, from a man, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded himself along with Khadija for a month, and that coincided with Ramadan. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and heard: Peace be upon you. She said: I thought it was the sudden appearance of the jinn. He said: Rejoice, for peace is good. Then another day he saw Jibril, peace be upon him, upon the sun, with one wing in the east and one wing in the west, and I was awed by him. She said: He set out intending his family, when there was Jibril, peace be upon him, between him and the door. He said: He spoke to me until I became at ease with him, then he promised me an appointment. He said: So I came to his appointment, and Jibril was withheld from me; then when he wanted to return, there he was, along with Mika'il, peace be upon him. Jibril descended to the earth while Mika'il remained between the heaven and the earth. He said: Jibril took me and laid me open for the sweetness of the nape, and split open my belly, and removed from it what Allah willed, then washed it in a basin of gold, then returned it therein, then turned me over as a vessel is turned over, then sealed upon my back until I felt the touch of the seal. Then he said to me: Read in the name of your Lord - though I had never read any book - and he seized my throat until I burst into weeping. Then he said to me: Read in the name of your Lord who created, created man from a clot, up to His saying, Exalted: what he knew not. He said: I never forgot anything thereafter. He said: Then he weighed me against a man and I outweighed him, then he weighed me against another and I outweighed him, then he weighed me against a hundred, and Mika'il said: His community has followed him, by the Lord of the Ka'ba. He said: Then I came to my dwelling, and no stone nor tree met me except that it said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, until I entered upon Khadija, and she said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. [FLAG: long eschatological narrative with unusual wording, e.g. seclusion with Khadija in Ramadan and weighing; translated literally]"
"1649","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Dhakwan, from A'isha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived when four - or five - days of Dhu al-Hijja had passed, and he entered upon me while angry. I said: Whoever has angered you, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah enter him into the Fire. He said: Do you not know that I commanded the people with a command, and they hesitate over it? Al-Hakam said: As if they were blocks of wood - had I known then what I know now, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal until I bought it, then I would have exited ihram as they exited ihram."
"1650","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt, from Irak, from A'isha, that when it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he ordered a seat to be brought and faced the qibla with it. [FLAG: terse/garbled matn, translated literally]"
"1651","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, saying: My father - meaning his father - informed me, from al-Sa'ib, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the house serpents - meaning of the snakes - except the short-tailed and the one with two stripes, for they snatch the eyesight and kill the fetus in women's bellies; whoever does not kill them is not of us."
"1652","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Ghalib, that A'isha said to Ammar: As for you, O Ammar, you have known what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after being married, or kills and so is killed."
"1653","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon the khumra."
"1654","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama and al-Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Yazid ibn Babanus, who said: We entered upon A'isha and mentioned the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: Abu Bakr entered and began moving between his cheeks with kisses, saying: O my Prophet, O my chosen one."
"1655","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn al-Ala' al-Yashkuri narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Sarj, from Abd al-Qays, narrated to me, from Imran ibn Hittan, who said: I heard A'isha saying, when judges were mentioned in her presence: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The just judge shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection and shall meet such severity of reckoning that he will wish he had never judged between two people even over a single date."
"1656","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Budayl al-Uqayli - a Basran, trustworthy, truthful - narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza', from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to open the prayer with the takbir and the recitation with All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds. When he bowed he would neither raise his head nor lower it, but between that; when he raised his head he would not prostrate until he stood straight; when he prostrated then raised his head he would not prostrate until he sat straight; he would spread his left foot and erect his right foot; he would say in every two rak'as: The greetings; he would forbid the heel of Satan and squatting like the squatting of the beast and the dog; and he would end the prayer with the taslim."
"1657","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad, who said: A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'as before Fajr, reciting therein to the extent of the Fatiha of the Book."
"1658","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from A'isha, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I presented to him meat or a bone, and I said: This is of what Barira brought us. He said: It is charity upon her, and a gift for us."
"1659","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sa'id al-Qurashi, of the descendants of Sa'id ibn al-As, narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: The fasting of the month of Ramadan as twenty-nine days was mentioned in the presence of A'isha and it was wondered at, so A'isha said: What amazes you of that? I did not fast with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-nine more often than I fasted thirty."
"1660","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me one day and said: Do you have anything? I said: No. He said: Then I fast. And he entered upon me another day and said: Do you have anything? I said: Yes. He said: Then I break my fast, even though I had resolved to fast."
"1661","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Imran ibn Bashir, from Salim Sabalan, who said: I heard A'isha saying to her brother: O Abd al-Rahman, perform ablution thoroughly, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"1662","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from A'isha, who said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina before he circumambulated the House."
"1663","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Shu'ayb al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, who said: I said to A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? She said: No, except when he came from his absence."
"1664","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Salt narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, who said: I said to A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) join between two suras? She said: No, except from the Mufassal."
"1665","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', who heard Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I asked A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast the known days of the month? She said: Yes."
"1666","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harun al-A'war narrated to us, from Budayl al-Uqayli, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from A'isha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he recited: Fa-rawhun wa rayhan."
"1667","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not wait, when he gave salam from the prayer, except to say: O Allah, You are Peace and from You is peace, blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"1668","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Mutarrif, from A'isha, that she said: I made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a black woolen cloak, and he wore it and it pleased him; then when he sweated in it and found the smell of the woolen garment, he cast it aside."
"1669","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from his aunt, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is not lawful for him until she tastes of his honey."
"1670","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr al-Makki narrated to me, saying: Safiyya bint Shayba narrated to us, saying: The Mother of the Believers A'isha narrated to us, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people return with two rites and I return with one rite? So he commanded my brother Abd al-Rahman, and he performed umra with me from al-Tan'im, mounting me behind him upon the camel on a hot night. I began uncovering my veil, and he struck at me with something in his hand. I said: Do you see anyone? Then I performed umra, and returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in his place, not having moved."
"1671","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr al-Makki of the family of Shayba, from Safiyya bint Shayba, who said: A'isha narrated to us, saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I pray inside the Ka'ba? He said: Pray in the Hijr, for it is part of the Ka'ba - or he said: part of the House."
"1672","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir al-Bajali, from Safiyya bint Shayba, from A'isha, who said: Such-and-such daughter of such-and-such, an Ansari woman, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, how is the bath from janaba? He said: One of you begins and performs ablution, beginning with the right side of her head, then the left, until she cleans the roots of her head. Then he said: Do you know what the roots of the head are? She said: The skin. He said: You have spoken truly; then she pours over the rest of her body. She said: O Messenger of Allah, and how is the bath from menstruation? He said: One of you takes her lote-tree leaves and her water, and purifies herself with it, perfecting the purification, then begins with the right side of her head, then the left, until she cleans the roots of the head, then pours over the rest of her body, then takes a musk-scented piece of cloth and purifies herself with it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I purify myself with it? So I said to her: Glory be to Allah! You follow the traces of blood."
"1673","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: ... narrated to us, from Safiyya, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with a sa' and perform ablution with a mudd. Thus in the Dar Hajar edition, with the editors noting the lacuna was effaced in the original. [FLAG: isnad lacuna marked ... in print; translated literally]"
"1674","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, saying: I heard al-Hasan ibn Muslim narrating from Safiyya, from A'isha, that a woman of the Ansar's hair fell out, and they wanted to add extensions to it, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cursed the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined."
"1675","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, that a man asked A'isha about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: No, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither dinar nor dirham, nor sheep nor camel, nor male nor female slave."
"1676","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Budayl al-Uqayli, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from a woman among them called Umm Kulthum, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eating food with six of his Companions, when a Bedouin came and ate it in two morsels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he mentioned the name of Allah it would have sufficed you; when one of you eats and forgets to mention the name of Allah, let him say: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end."
"1677","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mihzam narrated to us, saying: Karima bint Hammam al-Ta'iyya informed me, saying: We were in the Sacred Mosque with A'isha therein, and we sat with her, when a woman said to her: O Mother of the Believers, what do you say concerning henna for dyeing? She said: My beloved did not love its smell."
"1678","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from his mother, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the skins of dead animals when tanned - or he said: purified."
"1679","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Jabr ibn Habib, from Umm Kulthum, from A'isha, that she was praying, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Upon you is supplication with the perfect comprehensive ones. When she finished she asked him about that, and he said: Say: O Allah, I ask You of all good, what I know of it and what I know not, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I know not; and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and whatever brings near to it of word or deed; O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and whatever brings near to it of word or deed; O Allah, I ask You of the good that Your servant and Messenger Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked You, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your servant and Messenger Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge in You; and whatever decree You decree for me - or he said: whatever matter - make its outcome guidance for me."
"1680","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid Abi al-Azhar al-Duba'i al-Qassam al-Rishk, from Mu'adha al-Adawiyya, who said: I said to A'isha: Does the menstruating woman make up the prayer? She said: Are you a Haruriyya? We used to menstruate at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); did we make it up?"
"1681","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid, saying: I heard Mu'adha saying: I asked A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha? She said: Yes, four rak'as, and he would add whatever Allah willed."
"1682","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid: I heard Mu'adha; I said to A'isha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast three days of the month? She said: Yes. I said: From which part of the month? She said: He would not care from which part he fasted."
"1683","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Mu'adha, from A'isha: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to bathe from a single vessel, until he would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"1684","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ishaq, from A'isha bint Talha, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a child of the Ansar to pray over him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, glad tidings to him, a sparrow among the sparrows of Paradise; he never did any evil nor knew of it. He said: O A'isha, do you not know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Paradise and created people for it, creating it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers; and He created the Fire and created people for it, creating it for them while they were in the loins of their fathers."
"1685","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from Umm Ja'far, who said: I asked A'isha about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He would pray four before Zuhr, lengthening the standing therein and perfecting the bowing and prostration therein; as for what he never abandoned, healthy or ill, present or absent, it was the two rak'as before Fajr."
"1686","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil narrated to us, from Buhayya, from A'isha, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the children of the polytheists, and he said: They are in the Fire, O A'isha. I said: What do you say concerning the children of the Muslims? He said: They are in Paradise, O A'isha. I said: And how, when they did not attain deeds and the pens did not run upon them? He said: Your Lord knows best what they would have done."
"1687","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Burayd - or Ibn Burd - narrated to us, from Umm Salim, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: How much blessing is in your house? Meaning one sheep or two."
"1688","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sakan ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Sariyya informed us, saying: A'isha narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss her while fasting."
"1689","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Asim, the freedman of Qurayba, informed me, saying: I heard Qurayba narrating from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, yet you fast continuously. He said: I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"1690","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Umara ibn Umayr, from his mother, from A'isha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man's child is of his earning, of the best of his earning, so eat of their wealth."
"1691","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman: I heard Amra narrating from A'isha: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'as - Shu'ba said: To the best of my knowledge he said: lightening them; Shu'ba doubted concerning his lightening them. A'isha said: So I say: He recites therein the Fatiha of the Book."
"1692","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of the thief is cut for a quarter dinar and upward."
"1693","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amra, from A'isha, that Zaynab bint Jahsh had prolonged bleeding for seven years, so she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded her to bathe and pray, and she would bathe for every prayer."
"1694","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umayya bint Abdullah, who said: I asked A'isha about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Whether you disclose what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will bring you to account for it, and I asked her about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Whoever does evil shall be recompensed for it. She said: You have asked me about something none has asked me since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: This is Allah's, Mighty and Majestic, requital of the servant for what befalls him, of fever and grief and calamity, even the goods he places in his sleeve and loses, then is alarmed for it and finds it in his bosom, until the servant emerges from his sins as red gold emerges from the furnace."
"1695","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, saying: Umm al-Mughira, a freedwoman of the Ansar, informed me, saying: I asked A'isha about silk worn by women, and she said: At the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we were clothed in garments called al-sira', in which there was silk."
"1696","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, saying: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"1697","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Hafsa, or from A'isha, or both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband."
"1698","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sakhr ibn Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: People would see dreams at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and narrate them to him, and he would say concerning them whatever Allah willed him to say. One night I said to myself: If there were good in you, you would see a dream as people see. Then I said: O Allah, if You know there is good in me, show me. When I slept I saw in my dream as if two angels came to me, in the hand of each a whip of iron, and they took me until they stood me over Hell, holding me by the arms, and Hell was folded up. I said: I seek refuge in Allah from Hell, until an angel came and said: You have not been frightened; you are an excellent man, were you to pray much. Ibn Umar said: When morning came I went to Hafsa and narrated it to her, and Hafsa narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Abdullah is a righteous man. Nafi' said: Thereafter Abdullah would pray much."
"1699","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Nafi' informed me, saying: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salama narrating from Umm Salama, from a woman of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a relative of hers died, so she called for yellow dye and began wiping with it, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three, except over a husband: four months and ten days. Malik narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi', from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, who said: I entered upon Zaynab bint Jahsh."
"1700","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Nafi' informed me, saying: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salama narrating from Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, that a relative of hers died, so she called for yellow dye and began wiping with it, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three, except over a husband: four months and ten days."
"1701","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim: I heard Amr ibn Aws; I heard Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan narrating from Umm Habiba, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rak'as in a day and night apart from the obligatory, a house shall be built for him in Paradise. Umm Habiba, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I have not abandoned them since. Anbasa said: I have not abandoned them since. Amr said: I have not abandoned them since. Al-Nu'man said: And I hardly ever leave them since."
"1702","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, that a man entered upon Umm Habiba, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she called for sawiq - or food - for him, then said to him: O son of my brother, perform ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ablution is due to what fire has altered - or he said: what fire has touched."
"1703","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih, saying: I heard Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, saying: I heard Abu Hurayra and Ibn Abbas differing concerning the woman whose husband dies while she is pregnant. Ibn Abbas said: The later of the two terms, while Abu Hurayra said: When she delivers what is in her womb, she becomes lawful. So they sent me to Umm Salama; I came to her and asked her, and she said: Subay'a bint al-Harith gave birth fifteen nights after her husband's death, and two men proposed to her, and she inclined to one of them, and they feared she would decide for herself, so they said: Husbands are not lawful for you. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Rather, husbands have become lawful for you, so marry whomever you wish."
"1704","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from his father, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he recited: Amalun ghayru salih."
"1705","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Dabba ibn Mihsan, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be rulers; you will recognize and disapprove. Whoever disapproves has freed himself, and whoever hates has become safe, but whoever is pleased and follows. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill their wicked ones? He said: No, so long as they pray."
"1706","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Nafi' al-Madani narrated to us, saying: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salama narrating from her mother Umm Salama, that a woman whose husband died complained of her eyes, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Shall she apply kohl? He said: No; one of you used to remain in her husband's house for a year - or he said: in the worn furnishings of her house for a year - then when a dog passed she would throw a dung, then go out. No, until four months and ten days pass."
"1707","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'as in her house after Asr, and she asked him about that, and he said: I was praying two rak'as after Zuhr, when a delegation came and occupied me."
"1708","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ayyub and Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed me, from al-Hasan, saying: Our mother informed us, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning Ammar: The rebellious party shall kill you."
"1709","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is the jihad of every weak one."
"1710","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Wahb, from Umm Salama, who said: Abu Bakr went out trading to Busra at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1711","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sakhr ibn Juwayriya narrated to us, from Nafi', from Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salama - saying: Umm Salama was the maternal aunt of Abd al-Rahman - who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the one who drinks in a vessel of silver only gargles the fire of Hell - or he said: as if he gargles in his belly the fire of Hell."
"1712","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jumhan, saying: Safina, the freedman of Umm Salama, informed me, saying: Umm Salama freed me, stipulating upon me that I serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as he lived."
"1713","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast two consecutive months joining between them except Sha'ban and Ramadan."
"1714","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith al-Qurashiyya, from Umm Salama, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam from the prayer, he would not remain in his seat except a little until he stood. Al-Zuhri said: We deem that was for the sake of the women, so that they might depart."
"1715","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi A'isha, from a freedman of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr, he would say: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, wholesome provision, and accepted deed."
"1716","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Amir ibn Abi Umayya, brother of Umm Salama, from Umm Salama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub, then bathe and fast. Sa'id said: So Abu Hurayra retracted his fatwa."
"1717","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, saying: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Umm Salama, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his house, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from slipping, or going astray, or wronging, or being wronged, or acting ignorantly, or ignorance being acted upon me."
"1718","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ka'b narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: I entered upon Umm Salama and said to her: Inform me of what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated with most. She said: The most frequent supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicate with this often? He said: The heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic; what He wills He keeps straight, and what He wills He causes to deviate."
"1719","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Umm Salama, who said: By Allah, he did not die - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - until most of his prayer was while sitting, and the most beloved deeds to him were those persisted in, even if little."
"1720","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kamil Abu al-Ala' narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would remove hair with depilatory, tending to his pubic area with his hand."
"1721","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Imran narrated to us, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, from Ubaydallah ibn al-Qibtiyya, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: A people shall advance intending the House, until when they are at a desert plain of the earth, the earth shall swallow them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, among them is the coerced! He said: They shall be raised upon their intentions."
"1722","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Wahb, the freedman of Abu Ahmad, from Umm Salama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was veiling myself, and said: One wrap, not two."
"1723","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Mulayka saying: Umm Salama heard the cry over A'isha, so she sent her slave girl: See what she has done. She came and said: She has passed away. She said: May Allah have mercy on her; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, she was the most beloved of all people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except her father."
"1724","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Umm Salama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two daughters or two sisters or two female relatives, and spends upon them until they suffice him, or Allah enriches them of His bounty, they shall be a shield for him from the Fire."
"1725","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Murra, the freedman of Umm Hani', from Fakhita - who is Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the conquest, in my house, and bathed, then prayed in a single garment wrapped in it."
"1726","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Harun ibn Umm Hani', from Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I called for a drink for him and he drank - or she said: he called for a drink and drank - then he handed it to me and I drank, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting, but I disliked refusing your leftover. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it was making up a day of Ramadan, then fast a day in its place, and if it was voluntary, then if you wish, make it up, and if you wish, do not make it up."
"1727","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad - Qays narrated to us, saying: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Salih, the freedman of Umm Hani', from Umm Hani', who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And you commit evil in your gatherings. He said: They used to pelt whoever passed by them and mock him; that is the evil they used to commit."
"1728","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ja'da - a man of Quraysh, son of Umm Hani', whom Simak ibn Harb used to narrate from, saying: The two sons of Umm Hani' informed me; Shu'ba said: So I met the better of the two, Ja'da, and he narrated to me - from Umm Hani', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, and she handed him a drink and he drank, then handed it to her and she drank, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voluntary faster is the trustee of himself - or the commander of himself - if he wishes he fasts, and if he wishes he breaks his fast. Shu'ba said: So I said to Ja'da: Did you hear it yourself from Umm Hani'? He said: Our family and Abu Salih, the freedman of Umm Hani', informed me from Umm Hani'."
"1729","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Salih, from Umm Hani', who said: I never saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I remembered folded sheets of paper, one upon another."
"1730","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Layla saying: No one informed me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying Duha except Umm Hani', for she narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered her house on the day of the conquest of Makka, bathed, and prayed eight rak'as; I never saw him pray a prayer lighter than it, except that he would complete the bowing and prostration."
"1731","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Warqa' ibn Umar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Umayma bint Ruqayqa, who said: I was among those who pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he took from us that we would not steal, the entire verse; so we said: O Messenger of Allah, take our pledge. He said: I do not shake hands with women, and my word to one woman is as my word to a hundred women."
"1732","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man, from Talha al-Yami, from a woman of Abd al-Qays, from the sister of Abdullah ibn Rawaha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Going out is obligatory upon every veiled woman, meaning for the two Eids."
"1733","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada: I heard Abu Ayyub, from Juwayriya, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on a Friday while she was fasting, and said: Did you fast yesterday? She said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow? She said: No. He said: Then break your fast."
"1734","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Husayn sent me to al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh to ask her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often perform ablution in their presence. So I came to her and asked her, and she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution, and he took fresh water for his head."
"1735","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed - or she said: performed ablution - with the leftover of her bath from janaba."
"1736","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymuna, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon the khumra."
"1737","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I said to Miqsam: I pray witr with three, then go out to prayer fearing it will escape me. He said: Witr is not valid except with five or seven. I informed Mujahid and Yahya ibn al-Jazzar of it, and they said to me: Ask him from whom? So I asked him, and he said: From the trustworthy, from the trustworthy, from Maymuna and A'isha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1738","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed at her place, and she brought him a towel and he threw it aside. Al-A'mash said: So I mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: The hadith is thus, and there is no harm in wiping with the towel; it is merely habit."
"1739","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed, he would move aside from the bathing place and wash his feet."
"1740","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Amir, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left my house, he would raise his head to the sky and say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from slipping, or going astray, or wronging, or being wronged, or acting ignorantly, or ignorance being acted upon me."
"1741","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid al-Ansariyya, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: {Indeed, it is a deed that is not righteous}."
"1742","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak and Kharija narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Shahr, from Asma, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever defends the honor of his brother in his absence, it becomes binding upon Allah to free him from the Fire."
"1743","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr, from Asma, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: Before his emergence there will be a year in which the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation, and a second year in which the sky withholds two thirds of its rain and the earth two thirds of its vegetation, and a third year in which the sky withholds all its rain and the earth all its vegetation, until no tooth-possessing nor hoof-possessing creature remains, and among his greatest trials is that he will say to a man: If I bring your mother and father back to life for you, will you know that I am your lord, and devils will appear to them in their likeness. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for some need, and when he returned the people of the house were weeping, so he took hold of the two doorposts and said: What is the matter? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you mentioned the Dajjal, and by Allah, one of us kneads his dough and hardly bakes it before fearing he will be put to trial, while you say foods will be drawn to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What suffices the angels will suffice the believer on that day. They said: But the angels neither eat nor drink, they only glorify. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of the believers on that day will be glorification, and if he emerges while I am among you, I will be his disputant, and if he emerges after me, Allah is my Caliph over every Muslim."
"1744","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid al-Makki, from Siba ibn Thabit, from Umm Kurz al-Kabiyya, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Leave the birds upon their roosts. He said: meaning omens."
"1745","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim al-Madani, the freedman of Nafi, the freedman of Umm Qays bint Mihsan al-Asadiyya, narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: Umm Qays bint Mihsan informed me, saying: I recall that I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he held my hand in one of the lanes of Madina, in which there was no house, until we reached Baqi al-Gharqad, and he said: O Umm Qays. So I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and joy to you. He said: Do you see this graveyard? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Seventy thousand will be raised from it, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness, entering Paradise without reckoning. Then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, and I? He said: And you. Then another stood and said: And I, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Ukkasha has preceded you to it."
"1746","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zama narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Umm Qays, who informed him that a small boy who had not yet begun to eat food urinated in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and sprinkled it over it, and did not wash it thoroughly. Al-Zuhri said: So the Sunna continued that the urine of infant boys who have not eaten food is sprinkled, and the Sunna continued that the urine of boys who have eaten food is washed."
"1747","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri, who said: We entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and asked her about the temporary marriage with women, and she said: We did it in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1748","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Fatima bint al-Mundhir, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that a woman asked, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about menstrual blood that gets on clothing, and he said: Scrape it off with water, and sprinkle what is around it."
"1749","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Musab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that Abu Bakr divorced his wife Qutayla in the pre-Islamic era, and she was the mother of Asma bint Abi Bakr, and she came to them during the truce period between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the disbelievers of Quraysh, and she gave Asma bint Abi Bakr earrings and other things as a gift, but she disliked accepting from her until she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Allah does not forbid you from those who did not fight you for religion}."
"1750","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Salama informed me that Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed him that Asma bint Abi Bakr informed him that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: There is nothing more jealous than Allah, mighty and majestic."
"1751","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that she said to al-Hajjaj: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us that among Thaqif there will be a liar and a destroyer; as for the liar we have seen him, and as for the destroyer, I think you are none but him."
"1752","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Abd Allah, the freedman of Asma bint Abi Bakr, that Asma used to say to her family on the night of Muzdalifa: Has the moon set? Has the moon set? And when they said yes, she said: Arise; thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send us forth."
"1753","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, that Asma bint Abi Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me at the time of the treaty with Quraysh, and she is desirous and a polytheist; shall I maintain ties with her? He said: Yes, maintain ties with your mother."
"1754","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Ibn Man, from the daughter of Haritha ibn al-Numan al-Ansari, who said: I recall that our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were one, and I learned Qaf, meaning Surah Qaf, only from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he preached."
"1755","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm informed me, saying: I and Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon Fatima bint Qays during the reign of the family of al-Zubayr, and we asked her about the woman divorced thrice, whether she has maintenance. She said: My husband divorced me thrice, and provided neither lodging nor maintenance for me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and I said: He has provided neither lodging nor maintenance for me. He said: He spoke the truth. Then he said: Observe your waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said: The Emigrants visit her, but observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a man blind of sight, and perhaps you may lay aside your garments or some of them. She said: So I did, and when my waiting period ended, Abu al-Jahm, a man of Quraysh, and Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan proposed to me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Abu al-Jahm, he is a man severe upon women, and as for Muawiya, he is a man with no wealth. She said: Then Usama ibn Zayd proposed to me, so I married him, and Allah blessed me in Usama."
"1756","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from al-Shabi, who said: We entered upon Fatima bint Qays and she offered us fresh dates called Ibn Tab and gave us barley drink to drink, and we asked her about the woman divorced thrice, where she observes her waiting period. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted me to observe my waiting period among my family, meaning to move, and on that day it was announced among the people: prayer in congregation, so I went out among the women who went out, and I was in the front row of the women, next to the last row of the men, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Some cousins of Tamim al-Dari boarded the sea, and their ship cast them upon a shore of the seashores, and there was a beast covered by its hair, and when we entered upon it, it said: I am al-Jassasa. Then it said: In that monastery there is one longing to see you. So we entered, and there was a man chained in iron with hardship, and he said: Has your companion emerged, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So we said: Yes. He said: Then follow him. Then he said: Inform me about the date-palms of Baysan, do they bear fruit? We said: Yes. He said: Inform me about the Lake of Tiberias, is it abundant in water? We said: Yes. He said: Inform me about the spring of Zughar, is it abundant in water? We said: Yes. Then he said: Indeed, if I emerge I will tread all lands except Makkah and Tayba. Fatima said: So I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say with his staff: Indeed, this is Tayba, pointing toward the land of Madina, and Makkah is Makkah."
"1757","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage: It is only this one, then remaining upon the backs of mats. He said: So all of them used to travel except Zaynab and Sawda, for they said: No mount shall move us after what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1758","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Harim, from Said ibn Jubayr and Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Dubaa bint al-Zubayr to make a stipulation in the Hajj, and she did so by the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1759","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, who said: The people disputed about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafa at Arafat, so Umm al-Fadl said: I will find out for you. So she sent a vessel containing milk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drank."
"1760","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from the son of the daughter of Anas ibn Malik, from his grandmother Umm Sulaym, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink from the mouth of a waterskin, so I cut it off, and said: None shall drink from it after him."
"1761","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Ikrima, who said: Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit differed about a woman who menstruates after having circumambulated the House on the day of sacrifice; Zayd said: Her last covenant must be with the House, while Ibn Abbas said: She may depart whenever she wishes. So the Ansar said: We will not follow you, O Ibn Abbas, while you oppose Zayd. So he said: Ask your companion Umm Sulaym. So she said: I menstruated after circumambulating the House, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to depart, and Safiyya menstruated, and Aisha said to her: You have detained us, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to depart."
"1762","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, who said: Zaynab al-Thaqafiyya, the wife of Abd Allah ibn Masud, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her not to touch perfume when she goes out to the last evening prayer."
"1763","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Abu Wail narrate from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Zaynab al-Thaqafiyya, the wife of Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the women: Give charity even from your jewelry. So Zaynab said to Abd Allah: Would it suffice me to place my charity upon you and upon the orphaned sons of my brother or my sister? And Abd Allah was of little means, so he said: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. Zaynab said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a woman of the Ansar called Zaynab who had come to ask about what I had come to ask about, so Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and do not tell him who we are: does it suffice me to place my charity upon the orphaned sons of my brother or the orphaned sons of my sister in my care? So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Which of the Zaynabs is she? He said: Zaynab the wife of Abd Allah ibn Masud, and Zaynab a woman of the Ansar. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Inform them both that they have two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity."
"1764","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Husayn al-Ahmasi, who said: My grandmother Umm Husayn al-Ahmasiyya informed me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If an Abyssinian slave is placed in authority over you, so long as he leads you by the Book of Allah, then listen to him and obey."
"1765","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Husayn, from his grandmother, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for those who shave thrice and for those who shorten once."
"1766","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a liar who reconciles between two people, and speaks good or conveys good."
"1767","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Abd Allah or Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, that Marwan sent to Busra bint Safwan asking her, and she narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"1768","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Hassan al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: My two grandmothers, Duhayba and Safiyya, the daughters of Ulayba, narrated to me, from their stepdaughter and the grandmother of their father, Qayla bint Makhrama, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr prayer when the dawn had split, while the stars were tangled in the sky, hardly distinguishable in the darkness of the night, and the men were hardly distinguishable."
"1769","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the beggar comes and stands at my door, and I have nothing to give him. He said: Give him even a burnt hoof."
"1770","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas say: I heard my grandmother, or my mother, narrate that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Jamra while the people crowded, and he said: O people, do not kill yourselves; throw with pebbles like those of khadhf."
"1771","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: My aunt Unaysa narrated to me, saying: Bilal and Ibn Umm Maktum used to call the adhan for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan. So we used to hold Ibn Umm Maktum back from the adhan, saying: Wait until we take sahur, wait until we take sahur, and between their two adhans there was only that this one descends and this one ascends."
"1772","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, who said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Qurashi say: Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent to Umm Maqil, a woman of Ashja, and the woman said: An Umra was due upon me, and my husband had dedicated a young camel of his in the path of Allah, so I asked him to give it to me to perform Umra upon it, and he said: I have dedicated it in the path of Allah. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj and Umra are of the path of Allah. So he commanded him to give it to her to perform Umra upon it. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj, or he said: suffices for a Hajj. Shuba said: Then Abu Bishr narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that only to that woman specifically."
"1773","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from the daughter of Khabbab, that she brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sheep, so he held it and milked it, and said: Bring me your largest vessel. So we brought him the dough bowl, and he milked into it until he filled it, then said: Drink, you and your neighbors."
"1774","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ishaq, from Zaynab, from Furaya, the sister of Abu Said, that her husband followed some hired laborers and they killed him, while she was in a village of the villages of Madina, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and sought permission to go to her sisters to observe her waiting period with them, so he permitted her. Then he called her, or she was called to him, and he said: Remain in the house in which the news of your husband reached you until the decree reaches its term."
"1775","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, who said: Umm Ruman, the mother of Aisha, narrated to me, saying: While I was sitting, a woman entered upon me and said: May Allah do such and such to so-and-so. So I said: What is with him? She said: He spread the talk, meaning he mentioned Aisha. So Aisha said: Has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard of this? She said: Yes. She said: Has Abu Bakr heard of this? She said: Yes. So she was seized by something, and she did not rise except with fever, so I cast my garments over her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: What is the matter with her? So I said: Fever with chills seized her. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps it is on account of talk she was told. So Aisha sat up and said: By Allah, if I swear you will not believe me, and if I speak you will not accept from me, and my example and yours is only like that of Yaqub and his sons: {And Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe}. He said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed her exoneration, and Aisha said: By the praise of Allah, not by your praise nor by the praise of anyone."
"1776","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn Zayd al-Ansari informed me, saying: I heard a freedwoman of ours called Layla narrate from her grandmother Umm Umara al-Ansariyya that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no fasting person at whose place food is eaten except the angels send blessings upon him until they are satisfied, and once he said: until they finish. End of the narrations of women."
"1777","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of the conquest fasting until he reached Kura al-Ghamim, with the people alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on foot and mounted, and that was in Ramadan, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, fasting has become hard upon some people, and they only look to what you do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a cup containing water, raised it, and drank while the people looked on. So some people fasted and some broke fast, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that some of them were fasting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those are the disobedient."
"1778","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Madina nine years without performing Hajj, then he announced Hajj to the people, and many people intended to go out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he set out until he reached Dhu al-Hulayfa, where Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, so she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and he said: Bathe, bind yourself with a cloth, then enter ihram. So she did. He said: When the breast of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) settled upon the open desert, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his voice in talbiya and we did also, intending nothing but Hajj. Jabir said: I looked as far as my sight reached before me, behind me, to my right and to my left, of people on foot and mounted. So we set out knowing nothing but Hajj, for which we had set out, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among us, while the Quran descended upon him and he knew its interpretation, and he acted only by what he was commanded. Until we reached Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with the Stone and touched it, then circumambulated seven times, trotting in three of them and walking in four. Then he recited this verse: {And take the Station of Ibrahim as a prayer place}. He said: He prayed two rakas; my father said: He used to like to recite in them the chapters of Tawhid: {Say, O disbelievers} and {Say, He is Allah, One}, though he did not mention that in the narration of Jabir. Then he returned to the narration of Jabir: He said: Then he came to the Corner and touched it. He said: Then he went out to al-Safa. He said: We begin with what Allah began with, and said: {Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the rites of Allah}. He said: He ascended al-Safa until the House appeared to him, and magnified Allah thrice and said: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death; in His hand is good, and He is over all things capable. Then he supplicated between that. He said: Then he descended and walked until he came to the belly of the valley, hastened until his feet rose in the valley, then walked until he came to al-Marwa, ascended until the House appeared to him, magnified thrice, and said: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, just as he did, meaning upon al-Safa. Then he descended and said: Whoever does not have the sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it an Umra; had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would have made it an Umra. So they exited ihram, and Ali ibn Abi Talib arrived from Yemen and saw the people had exited ihram, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters ihram. He said: I have the sacrificial animal with me, so do not exit ihram. He said: So Ali entered upon Fatima, and she had applied kohl and worn dyed garments, so he disapproved of that and said: Who commanded you with this? She said: My father commanded me. Muhammad ibn Ali said: Ali used to narrate in Iraq: I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining against Fatima about what she mentioned, and he said: She spoke the truth; I commanded her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it thrice. When it was the day of sacrifice, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed sixty-three camels, and Ali sacrificed what remained, and they were a hundred camels. He took a piece from each camel, cooked, and he and Ali ate and drank of the broth. And Suraqa ibn Malik ibn Jushum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever? He said: No, rather forever; Umra has entered into Hajj. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers."
"1779","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my Ummah. He said: So Jabir said to me: Whoever is not of the people of major sins, what has he to do with intercession."
"1780","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaida narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: I walked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a woman of the Ansar, and she slaughtered a sheep for him and brought us food, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate and we ate. Then we stood for Zuhr, none of us performing ablution. Then we were brought the remainder of the sheep, and we dined from it, and Asr came, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and we stood and prayed, none of us touching water."
"1781","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaida narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: At what time of the night do you perform witr? He said: At the beginning of the night after the night prayer. And he said to Umar: At what time do you perform witr? He said: At the end of the night. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: You have taken the firm hold, and said to Umar: You have taken strength."
"1782","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaida narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded Hamza in a single garment. Jabir said: That garment was a striped cloak."
"1783","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaida narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who said: A man died, so we washed him, embalmed him, and shrouded him, then we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray over him. He stepped some steps, then said: Is there a debt upon him? We said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. So Abu Qatada said: O Messenger of Allah, his debt is upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are upon you as the right of the creditor, and the deceased is absolved. He said: Yes. So he prayed over him. Then he met him the next day and said: What happened to the two dinars? He said: O Messenger of Allah, he only died yesterday. Then he met him the next day and said: What happened to the two dinars? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have paid them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now you have cooled his skin."
"1784","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zaida narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: I walked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a woman of the Ansar, and she slaughtered a sheep for them, and we were brought that food, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter upon you. Then Abu Bakr entered. Then he said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter upon you. Then Umar entered. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of Paradise will enter upon you; O Allah, if You will, make him Ali. Then Ali entered."
"1785","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who marries without the permission of his master is a fornicator."
"1786","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated to us, saying: Ata narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of the fourth, with four days passed of Dhu al-Hijja, all of us entering ihram for Hajj. He commanded us, so we circumambulated the House, prayed two rakas, and hastened between al-Safa and al-Marwa. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exit ihram. We said: O Messenger of Allah, exit for what? He said: An exit like what is lawful for one out of ihram, of women and perfume. So women were approached and censers diffused fragrance. He said: And it reached him that some of them said: Shall one of us go to Mina with his member dripping semen? So he addressed them, praised Allah and glorified Him, then said: Had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal, and had I not driven it I would have exited ihram myself; so take your rites. Jabir said: So the people remained in their state of release until the day of Tarwiya, when they entered ihram for Hajj. The sacrifice was upon whoever found it, and fasting upon whoever did not find it. And he shared among them in their sacrifices: a camel for seven and a cow for seven. And their circumambulation of the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa was a single circumambulation and a single hastening, for their Hajj and their Umra."
"1787","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor has more right to the preemption of his neighbor; it is awaited for him even if he is absent, when their road is one."
"1788","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Rabah ibn Abi Maruf narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"1789","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Rabah narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that pregnant captive women be approached."
"1790","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, who heard Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A life-grant is permissible."
"1791","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: I said to Jabir: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) line up in prayer over the Negus? He said: Yes, and I was in the second row."
"1792","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, saying: One who heard Ata narrated to me, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce for one who has not married, nor freeing for one who does not own."
"1793","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the date-palms, with Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and reached his son Ibrahim while he was breathing his last. He placed the boy in his lap and wept. So Abd al-Rahman said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you forbid us from weeping? He said: I did not forbid weeping; I only forbade two depraved voices: the sound of a wind instrument at a blessing, the wind instrument of Satan and amusement, and a voice at a calamity, tearing garments and the wail of Satan; this is but mercy."
"1794","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qays, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before stoning. He said: Stone, and there is no harm."
"1795","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram for Hajj, and he said: Whoever of you wishes, let him make it an Umra, and whoever has the sacrificial animal with him cannot make it an Umra."
"1796","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Talha narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bury a man at night."
"1797","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A life-grant belongs to the one to whom it was granted."
"1798","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, saying: I asked Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman: Which Quran was revealed first? He said: {O you wrapped up}. I said: It has reached me that the first revealed was: {Read in the name of your Lord who created}. So Abu Salama said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah: Which Quran was revealed first? So he said to me: {O you wrapped up}. I said: It has reached me that the first revealed was: {Read in the name of your Lord who created}. So Jabir said: I inform you only of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. He said: I secluded myself in Hira, and when I completed my seclusion I departed, and when I descended into the valley I was called. I looked before me, to my right, to my left, and behind me, and saw nothing. Then I raised my head, and there he was upon a throne between heaven and earth, and I was struck with terror from him. Abu Dawud said: meaning I fell down from it. He said: So I came to Khadija, or he said: I came to my family, and said: Wrap me, wrap me. So I was wrapped, and cold water was poured over me. Then I was come to and it was said: {O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify}."
"1799","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then revelation paused."
"1800","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is granted a life-grant, it belongs to him and to his descendants after him."
